WEBVTT

1
00:02:54.474 --> 00:02:56.112
You know, Paan Singh killed...

2
00:02:56.176 --> 00:02:58.349
nine Gujjars in broad daylight.

3
00:02:58.411 --> 00:03:00.357
He was avenging his brother's death.

4
00:03:00.413 --> 00:03:02.222
And the cops are
completely helpless now.

5
00:03:02.315 --> 00:03:04.591
What can the cops do anyway?
If the cops are east...

6
00:03:04.651 --> 00:03:06.460
then Paan Singh is west.

7
00:03:06.653 --> 00:03:08.997
They say that
he used to be in the Army.

8
00:03:14.127 --> 00:03:16.164
Hey, give me a cigarette...

9
00:03:19.499 --> 00:03:20.603
The entire packet.

10
00:03:24.704 --> 00:03:25.978
Here's, your money.

11
00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:29.313
There's some hanky-panky going on!

12
00:03:29.375 --> 00:03:31.412
You look pretty pleased.

13
00:03:32.145 --> 00:03:33.624
You ain't seen nothing yet!

14
00:03:34.414 --> 00:03:35.984
Look out for my photo
on the first page of the newspaper.

15
00:03:36.082 --> 00:03:37.584
If it is not printed...

16
00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:39.186
then I'll eat the food
you feed your dogs.

17
00:03:39.285 --> 00:03:40.263
Why?

18
00:03:40.353 --> 00:03:42.299
Have you joined Paan Singh's gang?

19
00:03:42.388 --> 00:03:45.130
How do you know this?
Keep it to yourself!

20
00:03:58.104 --> 00:04:00.414
- The guy wearing the blue shirt?
- Yes.

21
00:04:02.041 --> 00:04:03.179
Yes?

22
00:04:03.476 --> 00:04:04.580
Greetings.

23
00:04:05.945 --> 00:04:07.049
Is he the journalist?

24
00:04:07.146 --> 00:04:07.988
Yes.

25
00:04:08.047 --> 00:04:09.958
I hope he won't squeal.

26
00:04:10.049 --> 00:04:11.153
Not at all.

27
00:04:11.684 --> 00:04:13.220
He's an army man.

28
00:04:13.319 --> 00:04:15.196
He is very particular
about punctuality.

29
00:04:15.288 --> 00:04:16.494
Absolutely.

30
00:04:20.126 --> 00:04:23.471
Till the task is completed
the girl stays with us.

31
00:04:25.465 --> 00:04:26.705
My dear...

32
00:04:26.799 --> 00:04:28.870
stay here with uncle...

33
00:04:28.968 --> 00:04:30.379
just for a little while.

34
00:04:30.436 --> 00:04:31.779
He'll give you sweets.

35
00:04:32.038 --> 00:04:33.642
You'll get your favourite sweet!

36
00:04:35.541 --> 00:04:37.680
He'll also show you
your favourite movie.

37
00:04:37.744 --> 00:04:38.722
Is that okay?

38
00:04:38.778 --> 00:04:39.984
Please look after her.

39
00:04:40.079 --> 00:04:41.080
Excuse me...

40
00:04:41.147 --> 00:04:42.217
hold on...

41
00:04:42.949 --> 00:04:45.691
Please keep this with you
and take care of her.

42
00:04:46.486 --> 00:04:47.590
Let's go?

43
00:04:48.321 --> 00:04:49.698
Is my sister safe here?

44
00:04:49.756 --> 00:04:51.463
That depends on you.

45
00:05:20.086 --> 00:05:21.326
Come on.

46
00:05:23.723 --> 00:05:24.929
Come...

47
00:05:25.224 --> 00:05:27.226
The journalist is here, Subedaar.

48
00:05:27.327 --> 00:05:29.136
I've frisked him.

49
00:05:29.228 --> 00:05:30.605
Listen, brother...

50
00:05:31.130 --> 00:05:32.700
How do I address him?

51
00:05:33.066 --> 00:05:34.409
Does 'sir' sound fine?

52
00:05:34.901 --> 00:05:36.039
Or...

53
00:05:36.102 --> 00:05:36.910
S... S... S...

54
00:05:37.003 --> 00:05:38.141
Subedaar?

55
00:05:59.792 --> 00:06:01.794
Thank you, Subedaar...

56
00:06:01.861 --> 00:06:03.863
for consenting to meet me.

57
00:06:05.264 --> 00:06:06.834
This interview...

58
00:06:06.966 --> 00:06:08.707
is very important to me.

59
00:06:09.068 --> 00:06:09.876
Hey...

60
00:06:09.969 --> 00:06:11.107
- What are you doing?
- What the...

61
00:06:11.170 --> 00:06:11.944
My N... N...

62
00:06:12.038 --> 00:06:14.109
I was just taking out my notebook.

63
00:06:14.173 --> 00:06:15.675
The way you moved your hands...

64
00:06:15.742 --> 00:06:16.948
I thought you had
a bomb in there.

65
00:06:17.043 --> 00:06:18.488
Let it be.

66
00:06:18.544 --> 00:06:20.046
Sir, I'm downstairs.

67
00:06:32.392 --> 00:06:33.996
Sit down.

68
00:06:34.060 --> 00:06:35.835
Any difficulty in
sitting on the floor?

69
00:06:38.664 --> 00:06:40.302
You are way younger than I am!

70
00:06:49.542 --> 00:06:51.522
You are Major Chauhan's nephew?

71
00:06:53.880 --> 00:06:55.223
Yes sir, he's my uncle.

72
00:06:55.281 --> 00:06:56.954
Why aren't you in the army?

73
00:06:57.750 --> 00:06:59.024
Sir, I...

74
00:06:59.419 --> 00:07:00.955
I'm passionate about writing.

75
00:07:01.854 --> 00:07:05.324
With your blessings
I hope to become a well known writer.

76
00:07:05.425 --> 00:07:08.668
You work at leisure
and it shows on your body!

77
00:07:09.328 --> 00:07:10.568
Get rid of it.

78
00:07:11.397 --> 00:07:13.900
From tomorrow, start running
four kilometers, everyday.

79
00:07:14.133 --> 00:07:15.237
Huh?

80
00:07:15.301 --> 00:07:16.678
Say, 'from tomorrow'.

81
00:07:16.769 --> 00:07:18.248
From T... T... tomorrow.

82
00:07:18.304 --> 00:07:20.875
- Say properly, 'from tomorrow'.
- From tomorrow.

83
00:07:26.345 --> 00:07:27.756
Shall we begin, sir?

84
00:07:32.718 --> 00:07:34.220
How did you become a dacoit?

85
00:07:42.528 --> 00:07:45.065
Are you a qualified journalist
or still training?

86
00:07:46.933 --> 00:07:48.970
Don't you know the
customs of this locality?

87
00:07:49.836 --> 00:07:51.941
In the ravines we're called rebels.

88
00:07:52.238 --> 00:07:54.240
Dacoits are found in the parliament.

89
00:07:54.273 --> 00:07:55.479
P... p... p...

90
00:07:56.576 --> 00:07:57.884
Forget it. The session's over.

91
00:07:58.110 --> 00:08:00.454
- N... no...
- Take your stuff and leave.

92
00:08:00.546 --> 00:08:02.389
- Subedaar, I... I... I'm sorry...
- I said it's over.

93
00:08:02.482 --> 00:08:04.052
It's over.

94
00:08:04.116 --> 00:08:05.561
What I meant was...

95
00:08:06.085 --> 00:08:07.689
Your C... Career...

96
00:08:10.256 --> 00:08:11.462
I mean...

97
00:08:12.258 --> 00:08:14.260
When did you
pick up the gun for the first time?

98
00:08:16.629 --> 00:08:18.302
That's the question.

99
00:08:22.835 --> 00:08:24.542
The British fled...

100
00:08:25.304 --> 00:08:26.874
and then...

101
00:08:29.275 --> 00:08:31.380
Pandit Nehru became
the Prime Minister.

102
00:08:32.512 --> 00:08:35.288
With a new beginning for India...

103
00:08:35.314 --> 00:08:37.590
I too started a new chapter
in my life.

104
00:08:52.498 --> 00:08:54.603
Ramcharan,
look who's coming this way?

105
00:08:54.667 --> 00:08:56.806
Daughter-in-law come here.

106
00:08:56.869 --> 00:08:58.075
Who is that?

107
00:08:58.137 --> 00:08:59.309
Who is he?

108
00:08:59.839 --> 00:09:01.182
Look who's coming!

109
00:09:12.218 --> 00:09:15.631
My son is home.

110
00:09:18.991 --> 00:09:21.972
He is an army man now!

111
00:09:24.263 --> 00:09:26.869
Look what I brought for you.

112
00:09:28.200 --> 00:09:30.908
If not us
at least think about your wife.

113
00:09:32.305 --> 00:09:34.478
I'm sorry, forgive me.

114
00:09:34.540 --> 00:09:36.110
Apologise to your wife!

115
00:09:36.208 --> 00:09:38.848
Now, can I get something to eat?

116
00:09:50.456 --> 00:09:52.060
Let me help you.

117
00:09:52.124 --> 00:09:53.398
Don't bother!

118
00:09:54.360 --> 00:09:56.101
I'm used to staying alone.

119
00:09:56.162 --> 00:09:57.368
Don't spoil me.

120
00:09:57.463 --> 00:09:59.534
If you are so used to it
then I'll go back tomorrow.

121
00:10:00.399 --> 00:10:01.503
Fine...

122
00:10:01.567 --> 00:10:03.808
you leave,
and I'll jump into the well.

123
00:10:19.819 --> 00:10:21.662
You've been hiding here.

124
00:10:22.154 --> 00:10:23.963
You're a good runner.

125
00:10:24.423 --> 00:10:26.027
Just like a rooster.

126
00:10:26.425 --> 00:10:29.531
Okay... swift as a cat!

127
00:10:32.598 --> 00:10:34.839
I've organized a village discourse...

128
00:10:34.934 --> 00:10:36.641
everyone is busy out there.

129
00:10:47.980 --> 00:10:49.357
Look at me.

130
00:11:06.132 --> 00:11:08.635
Did you also think I had died?

131
00:11:09.235 --> 00:11:11.374
Don't say that.

132
00:11:13.172 --> 00:11:15.083
I had shown your
horoscope to the priest.

133
00:11:16.108 --> 00:11:19.988
He said,
you were a born wanderer.

134
00:11:20.346 --> 00:11:21.791
But I knew...

135
00:11:22.481 --> 00:11:24.483
no matter what...

136
00:11:24.583 --> 00:11:26.688
you would come back to me.

137
00:11:32.658 --> 00:11:34.069
This is the army,
not a government office...

138
00:11:34.126 --> 00:11:35.696
where you can do as you please.

139
00:11:35.961 --> 00:11:37.702
Why are you late by two days?

140
00:11:37.763 --> 00:11:39.504
Sir, my mother was ill.

141
00:11:39.598 --> 00:11:41.009
Sir, I was getting married.

142
00:11:41.100 --> 00:11:42.807
The Army comes first,
and family later.

143
00:11:42.902 --> 00:11:43.812
And you?

144
00:11:43.903 --> 00:11:46.179
Sir, I had to harvest
the standing crop.

145
00:11:46.238 --> 00:11:48.081
Soon you won't be standing either!

146
00:11:48.174 --> 00:11:51.018
Run ten rounds
with luggage on your head.

147
00:11:58.918 --> 00:12:00.397
Left, right, left.

148
00:12:00.453 --> 00:12:02.194
Attention!

149
00:12:04.156 --> 00:12:05.897
Ten...
I did ten rounds, sir.

150
00:12:09.995 --> 00:12:11.406
You think I'm an idiot?

151
00:12:11.497 --> 00:12:14.137
I'm a fast runner.
I have no problem with running.

152
00:12:14.200 --> 00:12:16.544
Great, then run another ten rounds.

153
00:12:16.769 --> 00:12:18.646
With or without my luggage, sir?

154
00:12:30.950 --> 00:12:32.952
Rakesh...

155
00:12:35.254 --> 00:12:36.494
Who is this guy?

156
00:12:36.555 --> 00:12:39.161
He's a new recruit,
Paan Singh Tomar.

157
00:12:41.260 --> 00:12:43.536
For the first time I've seen
someone enjoying his punishment.

158
00:12:52.938 --> 00:12:54.178
That's 37 rupees.

159
00:12:54.240 --> 00:12:57.153
How will you manage
with just two rupees?

160
00:12:57.209 --> 00:12:59.189
The military takes care
of my needs.

161
00:12:59.245 --> 00:13:00.519
My wife has just
delivered a baby girl.

162
00:13:00.579 --> 00:13:01.990
Congratulations!

163
00:13:02.748 --> 00:13:04.853
I need to take care of
their needs now.

164
00:13:14.593 --> 00:13:18.769
Do you eat to live?
Or live to eat?

165
00:13:19.899 --> 00:13:21.776
This is the bread for living...

166
00:13:22.101 --> 00:13:23.580
and this is the bread for eating.

167
00:13:24.103 --> 00:13:25.309
Take some?

168
00:13:25.838 --> 00:13:27.545
Take it.

169
00:13:30.242 --> 00:13:31.380
Paan Singh...

170
00:13:31.443 --> 00:13:33.013
this is a battalion,
not a bachelor's party.

171
00:13:33.112 --> 00:13:35.956
We're short on supplies
and you will starve us to death.

172
00:13:36.048 --> 00:13:37.391
I have a large appetite.

173
00:13:37.449 --> 00:13:40.862
Get into sports,
there is no dearth of food there.

174
00:13:47.326 --> 00:13:49.966
Bye, ma'am.
Have a great time in Gwalior.

175
00:13:53.933 --> 00:13:56.209
The British left behind
two great things, sir.

176
00:13:56.769 --> 00:13:58.339
First is discipline...

177
00:13:58.604 --> 00:14:00.481
and the second is ice-cream.

178
00:14:00.539 --> 00:14:02.075
I've got some for you.

179
00:14:02.842 --> 00:14:04.822
Take some home,
ma'am will love it.

180
00:14:04.910 --> 00:14:06.617
No, no...
By the time I get home...

181
00:14:06.712 --> 00:14:09.192
it will become a milkshake!

182
00:14:09.281 --> 00:14:10.453
Sir...

183
00:14:12.551 --> 00:14:13.495
Take me into sports.

184
00:14:13.586 --> 00:14:15.224
There is no restriction
on food there.

185
00:14:15.287 --> 00:14:16.459
Sports?

186
00:14:16.722 --> 00:14:17.860
Which sport?

187
00:14:17.923 --> 00:14:20.403
Anything, sir.
I even run very fast.

188
00:14:20.492 --> 00:14:22.233
Oh really?

189
00:14:22.294 --> 00:14:23.637
Yes, I love to run.

190
00:14:23.662 --> 00:14:26.939
Fine, if you deliver this ice-cream
to the Major's house...

191
00:14:27.032 --> 00:14:28.238
before it melts!

192
00:14:28.300 --> 00:14:29.677
Then you are a sportsman.

193
00:14:29.768 --> 00:14:30.906
The address, sir?

194
00:15:10.976 --> 00:15:13.513
The Major has sent this.

195
00:15:13.612 --> 00:15:14.989
You can check it's not melted.

196
00:15:15.514 --> 00:15:16.993
What is the time now?

197
00:15:17.049 --> 00:15:18.722
It's nine o'clock. Why?

198
00:15:19.485 --> 00:15:21.396
Tell him I was here in four minutes.

199
00:15:21.453 --> 00:15:22.693
What?

200
00:15:48.547 --> 00:15:49.890
Paan Singh... run!!

201
00:15:49.949 --> 00:15:51.155
You're supposed to
run at the signal...

202
00:15:51.216 --> 00:15:54.163
not recite a prayer, you idiot!
Now run!

203
00:15:57.890 --> 00:16:00.871
He is one who delivered
the ice cream in four minutes!

204
00:16:38.664 --> 00:16:41.372
Congratulations, Paan Singh!
You're the runner-up.

205
00:16:41.467 --> 00:16:42.741
Sir, are these for the athletes?

206
00:16:42.801 --> 00:16:45.645
Paan Singh has potential.

207
00:16:46.372 --> 00:16:49.751
But he wants to be
a sportsman to satisfy his hunger!

208
00:16:49.808 --> 00:16:52.118
Don't think he is
interested in sports.

209
00:16:59.518 --> 00:17:01.259
Hit it hard.

210
00:17:02.454 --> 00:17:04.400
Harder, now.

211
00:17:14.233 --> 00:17:14.938
Load them up.

212
00:17:15.034 --> 00:17:16.980
My father fought
against the British...

213
00:17:17.069 --> 00:17:19.379
and he sent me here...

214
00:17:19.471 --> 00:17:21.041
to serve the country.

215
00:17:21.473 --> 00:17:24.249
I can't do this.
I can't operate a gun.

216
00:17:24.710 --> 00:17:26.246
You are an idiot.
Say, 'yes'.

217
00:17:27.946 --> 00:17:29.152
Say 'yes'.

218
00:17:29.181 --> 00:17:30.319
Yes, sir.

219
00:17:30.382 --> 00:17:32.157
It's easy.

220
00:17:32.217 --> 00:17:33.924
Strap on the gun...
shut one eye...

221
00:17:33.986 --> 00:17:35.226
aim at your target
and pull the trigger.

222
00:17:35.320 --> 00:17:36.390
It's as simple as that.

223
00:17:36.455 --> 00:17:37.627
What's going on here?

224
00:17:38.791 --> 00:17:41.271
He's new here.
I'm teaching him to shoot.

225
00:17:41.627 --> 00:17:42.799
He's new here...

226
00:17:42.861 --> 00:17:44.033
and you were born
with a gun?

227
00:17:44.096 --> 00:17:46.098
The gun and I share
along relationship.

228
00:17:46.198 --> 00:17:47.734
My uncle owns four Mark-3 guns.

229
00:17:47.833 --> 00:17:50.871
Is that so?
Then show me your skills.

230
00:17:52.304 --> 00:17:54.284
Nobody else fires!

231
00:18:01.980 --> 00:18:03.152
On your feet!

232
00:18:04.783 --> 00:18:05.887
Sir.

233
00:18:06.251 --> 00:18:07.423
Where are you from?

234
00:18:07.519 --> 00:18:09.055
From Bhidosa,
in Morena district.

235
00:18:09.488 --> 00:18:12.765
I see, the Chambal Valley.
Dacoit area!

236
00:18:12.825 --> 00:18:14.270
Not dacoits. They are rebels.

237
00:18:14.359 --> 00:18:17.897
My uncle was a rebel too,
and a respected one.

238
00:18:18.263 --> 00:18:20.209
The cops have not been
able to nab him.

239
00:18:23.068 --> 00:18:24.376
Recruit Paan Singh...

240
00:18:25.237 --> 00:18:27.410
was your uncle a dacoit?

241
00:18:27.473 --> 00:18:29.475
Not a dacoit. He was a rebel.

242
00:18:29.541 --> 00:18:30.986
He was a good man.

243
00:18:31.076 --> 00:18:34.182
Stick to the question.

244
00:18:36.715 --> 00:18:38.160
There are no records...

245
00:18:38.217 --> 00:18:41.130
but have you ever
been to jail?

246
00:18:41.186 --> 00:18:44.827
Not even my uncle.
The police cannot catch us.

247
00:18:47.759 --> 00:18:51.036
I asked you to stick to the question.

248
00:18:52.264 --> 00:18:54.471
Do you trust the government?

249
00:18:54.533 --> 00:18:56.206
No, sir, the government is a crook.

250
00:18:56.635 --> 00:18:59.479
That's why, I'm in the Army
and not a government servant.

251
00:19:00.772 --> 00:19:03.548
Except the army,
everyone is a swindler.

252
00:19:05.477 --> 00:19:07.286
Can you give your life
for your country?

253
00:19:07.346 --> 00:19:08.950
Yes, and I can take lives too.

254
00:19:09.081 --> 00:19:10.685
This country is our motherland...

255
00:19:10.749 --> 00:19:13.787
If anyone dares harm my mother,
how can I bear it?

256
00:19:15.387 --> 00:19:17.731
The Army means discipline.

257
00:19:18.090 --> 00:19:22.038
You need to obey the orders
of your officer.

258
00:19:22.094 --> 00:19:24.574
Will you obey every order?

259
00:19:25.797 --> 00:19:28.403
Sir, I'm a fourth grade drop out.

260
00:19:28.934 --> 00:19:31.039
I've learnt more from
experience than books.

261
00:19:31.470 --> 00:19:33.472
If an officer like you
gives me an order...

262
00:19:34.239 --> 00:19:35.650
I'd give up my life.

263
00:19:38.644 --> 00:19:42.558
But, sir, a few officers here
are just for namesake.

264
00:19:42.581 --> 00:19:44.356
They are good for nothing.

265
00:19:46.285 --> 00:19:48.856
I'm not too sure
about their orders.

266
00:19:49.254 --> 00:19:50.995
Sir, let me talk to him.

267
00:19:51.056 --> 00:19:53.332
Major Masand,
this is the man you were recommending.

268
00:19:53.392 --> 00:19:57.636
Have you heard what he is saying?
He shouldn't even be here.

269
00:19:57.696 --> 00:20:00.302
- I still have my doubts.
- I'm trying to understand.

270
00:20:00.399 --> 00:20:03.005
Sir, what he is trying to say
is something different...

271
00:20:03.068 --> 00:20:04.945
Did I say something wrong, sir?

272
00:20:05.437 --> 00:20:09.317
Paan Singh, it's okay.
You may wait outside.

273
00:20:16.515 --> 00:20:20.019
Check out his attitude.
He's got a rebel for an uncle.

274
00:20:20.118 --> 00:20:21.358
Great!

275
00:20:21.420 --> 00:20:24.162
- Army officers are useless.
- Sir...

276
00:20:24.223 --> 00:20:28.103
He is the best recipe for a mutiny!
We have to do something about him.

277
00:20:28.193 --> 00:20:29.365
I have an idea...

278
00:20:29.428 --> 00:20:33.467
we should send him to
the Army Physical Training Center.

279
00:20:33.899 --> 00:20:37.108
He can run as much as he wants to.
That will cool his temper.

280
00:20:37.202 --> 00:20:39.045
We should use him to our advantage.

281
00:20:40.806 --> 00:20:43.252
You haven't seen him run yet.

282
00:20:57.389 --> 00:20:58.993
Good morning...

283
00:20:59.057 --> 00:21:02.869
Looks like you stepped out of bed
and onto the ground!

284
00:21:02.961 --> 00:21:04.565
- Good morning, sir.
- Good morning...

285
00:21:04.963 --> 00:21:08.536
- Greetings Gurveer, everything okay?
- Greetings to you too.

286
00:21:08.634 --> 00:21:10.079
Done with the warm up?

287
00:21:10.202 --> 00:21:12.739
It makes no difference to me.
I'm always ready.

288
00:21:13.005 --> 00:21:15.281
All of you here,
for the 5000 meter race.

289
00:21:15.674 --> 00:21:17.449
Everyone on your feet!

290
00:21:17.876 --> 00:21:19.480
Let's begin the race!

291
00:21:22.948 --> 00:21:25.224
- Jai Hind, coach.
- Jai Hind!

292
00:21:25.317 --> 00:21:27.558
Aren't you from Bengal Engineers?

293
00:21:27.619 --> 00:21:28.461
Yes, sir.

294
00:21:28.553 --> 00:21:29.725
You want to run the 5000 meter?

295
00:21:29.788 --> 00:21:30.596
Yes, sir.

296
00:21:30.656 --> 00:21:31.828
Let's go.

297
00:21:32.157 --> 00:21:33.636
What's your name?

298
00:21:34.359 --> 00:21:35.895
My name is Paan Singh Tomar, sir.

299
00:21:35.994 --> 00:21:38.406
Athletes... on your mark!

300
00:23:03.882 --> 00:23:05.623
- Jai Hind, sir.
- Jai Hind!

301
00:23:06.385 --> 00:23:09.366
Hold on, Paan Singh.
I need to talk to you.

302
00:23:09.421 --> 00:23:10.593
About what?

303
00:23:10.655 --> 00:23:13.158
I need to discuss
something very important.

304
00:23:13.191 --> 00:23:14.397
Come along.

305
00:23:14.860 --> 00:23:17.397
Don't mind my words.

306
00:23:17.462 --> 00:23:19.567
- Greetings, coach.
- Greetings.

307
00:23:20.065 --> 00:23:23.376
I suggest you don't run
the 5000 meters race.

308
00:23:23.468 --> 00:23:24.776
Don't run?!

309
00:23:25.971 --> 00:23:27.848
Not take part in the
5000 meter race?

310
00:23:30.308 --> 00:23:32.982
But I've been sent here for this race.

311
00:23:33.412 --> 00:23:35.949
I have other plans for you.

312
00:23:36.648 --> 00:23:39.458
You are a good runner,
with a good stamina.

313
00:23:39.551 --> 00:23:42.225
You should run a different race.

314
00:23:45.190 --> 00:23:46.999
All these months
that's what I've been practicing for.

315
00:23:47.058 --> 00:23:48.503
The Defense Meet is in two months...

316
00:23:48.560 --> 00:23:49.937
where I have to win a medal.

317
00:23:49.995 --> 00:23:51.668
Why are you stuck on
the Defense Meet?

318
00:23:51.730 --> 00:23:54.108
I want to make you a
national champion.

319
00:23:54.166 --> 00:23:56.112
So why not in 5000 meters?

320
00:23:58.670 --> 00:23:59.774
Listen to me.

321
00:23:59.871 --> 00:24:03.375
If you run the 5000 meter,
Gurveer will lose...

322
00:24:03.442 --> 00:24:05.388
How does this concern me?

323
00:24:05.444 --> 00:24:06.821
Listen...

324
00:24:06.912 --> 00:24:10.257
My daughter is married to
Gurveer's brother.

325
00:24:11.917 --> 00:24:13.487
My daughter is already suffering.

326
00:24:14.119 --> 00:24:16.258
If Gurveer loses, his brother will...

327
00:24:16.388 --> 00:24:18.197
take it out on my daughter.

328
00:24:18.256 --> 00:24:19.963
I get it, coach.

329
00:24:22.861 --> 00:24:24.932
Since this concerns
my teacher's daughter...

330
00:24:24.996 --> 00:24:28.000
I can run on hot coals now.

331
00:24:31.269 --> 00:24:32.839
Bless you, my son.

332
00:24:33.672 --> 00:24:37.814
Not fire, you will run on water.

333
00:24:38.043 --> 00:24:39.215
On water?

334
00:24:39.277 --> 00:24:41.757
You will run the steeplechase!

335
00:24:41.847 --> 00:24:43.884
Steeplechase.

336
00:24:46.284 --> 00:24:47.456
Yes, sir.

337
00:24:48.286 --> 00:24:49.560
I will run.

338
00:25:09.040 --> 00:25:14.456
Earlier, the steeplechase was
a race meant for horses.

339
00:25:14.980 --> 00:25:17.290
Later, this was
introduced into athletics.

340
00:25:18.450 --> 00:25:19.793
Watch carefully...

341
00:25:21.319 --> 00:25:25.199
There are 28 hurdles.

342
00:25:25.624 --> 00:25:31.631
And 7 water pits, which you
have to cross to finish the race.

343
00:25:33.131 --> 00:25:39.013
If horses and donkeys can do it
then you are way better than them!

344
00:26:00.892 --> 00:26:04.965
Praise the Lord!

345
00:26:17.609 --> 00:26:18.815
Very good.

346
00:26:19.444 --> 00:26:21.583
Remember you're training for
the National Games.

347
00:27:25.243 --> 00:27:30.022
Now, the last track and field event.
The 3000 meter steeplechase.

348
00:27:30.081 --> 00:27:33.255
Athletes on your mark!

349
00:27:33.318 --> 00:27:36.356
Use your stamina wisely.

350
00:27:36.454 --> 00:27:38.900
Why do you keep looking behind you?

351
00:27:38.990 --> 00:27:41.732
Do you think
you're in a wedding procession?

352
00:27:46.765 --> 00:27:48.005
What's wrong?

353
00:27:48.099 --> 00:27:49.806
Sir, I'm thirsty.
I'd like some water.

354
00:27:49.901 --> 00:27:51.539
Have you lost it?

355
00:27:51.603 --> 00:27:54.311
It's a race,
not a pissing competition!

356
00:28:56.601 --> 00:29:01.380
Paan Singh, if you lose this race,
you motherfucker...

357
00:29:01.439 --> 00:29:04.943
I will bury you right here
in this ground.

358
00:29:13.885 --> 00:29:15.956
What are you doing?!

359
00:29:57.462 --> 00:30:00.136
- The time?
- It's 9:12:04.

360
00:30:00.231 --> 00:30:03.769
You clocked 9:12:04.
A new national record.

361
00:30:04.035 --> 00:30:07.278
Congratulations...
this is unbelievable!

362
00:30:09.007 --> 00:30:11.283
You're the national champion.

363
00:30:11.376 --> 00:30:12.855
You broke the record.

364
00:30:12.911 --> 00:30:15.858
I knew you were
champion material!

365
00:30:19.083 --> 00:30:21.461
What's the matter?
Aren't you happy?

366
00:30:23.621 --> 00:30:25.498
Coach, the thing is...

367
00:30:25.890 --> 00:30:27.528
you are my teacher.

368
00:30:27.625 --> 00:30:29.468
But next time you shout at me...

369
00:30:29.627 --> 00:30:31.334
don't abuse my mother!

370
00:30:34.833 --> 00:30:37.074
You know it's a habit, Paan Singh.

371
00:30:37.168 --> 00:30:38.772
I also have a habit.

372
00:30:38.837 --> 00:30:40.942
I pull the trigger
when I hear abuses.

373
00:30:41.005 --> 00:30:43.178
I love my mother a lot.

374
00:31:24.148 --> 00:31:27.254
Hanumanta, go get
some lemon toffees.

375
00:31:28.586 --> 00:31:30.691
The shop here is no good.

376
00:31:31.089 --> 00:31:34.366
You get better ones
near the bus stop.

377
00:31:36.527 --> 00:31:38.268
Take your sister along.

378
00:31:50.208 --> 00:31:52.210
I didn't get anything for you.

379
00:31:53.044 --> 00:31:56.856
Can you make something sweet?
I have some good news to share.

380
00:31:56.915 --> 00:31:59.589
Tell me the good news,
then I'll make the sweets.

381
00:32:00.551 --> 00:32:02.360
What if I don't like the news?

382
00:32:02.420 --> 00:32:05.401
I have been promoted.
You are now the wife of a Subedaar.

383
00:32:05.490 --> 00:32:07.401
I broke the National record.

384
00:32:07.926 --> 00:32:10.429
What have you broken this time?

385
00:32:10.528 --> 00:32:13.031
Every time you go out,
you break something.

386
00:32:14.732 --> 00:32:17.611
Idiot! When will you learn?

387
00:32:17.802 --> 00:32:19.713
I haven't broken anything. It means...

388
00:32:21.739 --> 00:32:23.616
I've set a new time record.

389
00:32:23.675 --> 00:32:24.949
Really?

390
00:32:26.144 --> 00:32:27.714
How would I know that?

391
00:32:37.922 --> 00:32:39.230
Let me go... no don't!

392
00:32:39.290 --> 00:32:40.166
Let me go...

393
00:32:40.224 --> 00:32:41.464
I said no!

394
00:32:53.171 --> 00:32:54.912
They're sending me abroad.

395
00:32:56.274 --> 00:32:57.719
Tokyo, Japan.

396
00:32:58.876 --> 00:33:01.379
Major athletes from
Asia will be present.

397
00:33:04.115 --> 00:33:06.857
What do you want from Tokyo?

398
00:33:10.888 --> 00:33:12.231
Come.

399
00:33:13.424 --> 00:33:15.267
- Going abroad?
- Yes.

400
00:33:17.028 --> 00:33:18.336
What do you want?

401
00:33:23.267 --> 00:33:27.773
I don't like the way
you run in shorts.

402
00:33:27.972 --> 00:33:29.645
The women stare at you.

403
00:33:30.375 --> 00:33:32.753
Should I run in my pajamas?

404
00:33:34.345 --> 00:33:35.881
What if I bring home
a Japanese wife?

405
00:33:36.681 --> 00:33:39.252
Which well will you jump into?

406
00:33:40.952 --> 00:33:42.932
I'll lie down on the rail tracks.

407
00:33:43.721 --> 00:33:45.132
Let me just kill you then.

408
00:33:46.524 --> 00:33:47.730
Shall I?

409
00:33:51.696 --> 00:33:53.607
The kids will be here.

410
00:33:53.664 --> 00:33:54.802
No...

411
00:33:54.832 --> 00:33:57.335
No... don't...

412
00:34:06.377 --> 00:34:07.583
Let go!

413
00:34:41.379 --> 00:34:44.053
Water... drinking water?

414
00:34:45.716 --> 00:34:47.252
Coach...

415
00:34:47.351 --> 00:34:48.352
do I need to wear these?

416
00:34:48.419 --> 00:34:49.557
Of course, it's necessary.

417
00:34:49.620 --> 00:34:52.999
Coach, with these nails,
the shoes will dig into the earth.

418
00:34:53.057 --> 00:34:54.798
- They are called spikes.
- What?

419
00:34:54.859 --> 00:34:56.998
Spikes! Come on...

420
00:34:57.061 --> 00:34:59.200
Indian athletes will participate
without spikes?

421
00:34:59.263 --> 00:35:00.503
Why didn't you give
these for practice?

422
00:35:00.598 --> 00:35:02.373
I've been running
wearing canvas shoes.

423
00:35:02.467 --> 00:35:05.846
Now, you're giving these to me
and that too, at the competition.

424
00:35:05.903 --> 00:35:09.510
So, the world should
mock Indian athletes?

425
00:35:09.574 --> 00:35:11.212
Look at the other athletes.

426
00:35:11.309 --> 00:35:12.287
Why should I?

427
00:35:12.343 --> 00:35:14.755
They get good food
and all the facilities.

428
00:35:14.779 --> 00:35:16.725
You expect us to win a medal
on two egg yolks?!

429
00:35:16.781 --> 00:35:17.816
What's your point?

430
00:35:17.915 --> 00:35:19.326
Whatever you want to make of it!

431
00:35:19.383 --> 00:35:21.761
Don't act smart! Get it?

432
00:35:21.819 --> 00:35:24.231
Wear the shoes and
take your position.

433
00:35:24.288 --> 00:35:27.565
Come on... you will definitely win!
Move it!

434
00:36:56.147 --> 00:36:58.252
That day I lost the race.

435
00:36:58.549 --> 00:37:00.790
I regret it to this day.

436
00:37:00.885 --> 00:37:02.364
And I always will.

437
00:37:02.853 --> 00:37:05.527
- Don't be upset.
- I had to take my shoes off.

438
00:37:05.623 --> 00:37:07.000
It's okay.

439
00:37:07.091 --> 00:37:10.334
They don't give us facilities.
They just keep asking for medals.

440
00:37:14.365 --> 00:37:15.605
You know English?

441
00:37:23.107 --> 00:37:25.747
I don't understand what
they are saying. You handle it.

442
00:37:26.711 --> 00:37:29.715
Sir, could you please
tell us your name?

443
00:37:29.814 --> 00:37:31.054
Oh?!

444
00:37:32.416 --> 00:37:33.486
Paan Singh Tomar.

445
00:37:34.352 --> 00:37:35.854
Paan Singh Tomar.

446
00:37:38.923 --> 00:37:41.233
Paan Singh Tomar, India.

447
00:37:41.726 --> 00:37:43.034
India.

448
00:37:43.694 --> 00:37:45.799
Paan Singh I love you.

449
00:37:45.863 --> 00:37:47.865
She is in love with you.

450
00:38:01.145 --> 00:38:02.488
All he's brought back
is dirty clothes!

451
00:38:02.580 --> 00:38:03.251
How is she?

452
00:38:03.347 --> 00:38:04.382
She's nice.

453
00:38:04.482 --> 00:38:05.620
Just nice?

454
00:38:05.716 --> 00:38:06.956
He has me to clean up after him.

455
00:38:07.051 --> 00:38:10.032
Did he go there for
a medal or a new wife!

456
00:38:10.087 --> 00:38:12.158
I'd almost decided
on settling there.

457
00:38:12.256 --> 00:38:13.667
What stopped you?

458
00:38:13.791 --> 00:38:15.395
Your cooking!

459
00:38:15.493 --> 00:38:17.530
The food there is terrible!

460
00:38:17.628 --> 00:38:20.108
No difference between
a dog and a duck.

461
00:38:20.197 --> 00:38:21.870
All you remembered,
was my cooking!

462
00:38:23.100 --> 00:38:25.774
Hanu, get some lemon toffee.

463
00:38:25.870 --> 00:38:28.612
They are not going anywhere.
Sit right here.

464
00:38:28.706 --> 00:38:31.550
- Here is the money.
- I said, you will not go.

465
00:38:31.642 --> 00:38:33.383
- Let the kids go.
- They aren't going!

466
00:38:33.477 --> 00:38:36.117
- Let them eat the toffee
- I said, you will not go.

467
00:38:36.247 --> 00:38:38.193
Didn't you hear me?
You won't go!

468
00:38:38.749 --> 00:38:40.751
Lemon toffees, my foot!

469
00:38:41.252 --> 00:38:42.595
They aren't going anywhere!

470
00:39:15.553 --> 00:39:18.159
Hanu, time you took
a break from studying.

471
00:39:18.255 --> 00:39:22.670
Go out for a while and
get my clothes from the tailor.

472
00:39:22.760 --> 00:39:27.038
Take your sister along.
She needs a new dress.

473
00:39:29.467 --> 00:39:32.175
Don't hurry with the measurements.

474
00:39:42.680 --> 00:39:44.853
So, you put the kids to work?!

475
00:39:46.117 --> 00:39:49.155
Were you really going to
bring that Japanese woman here?

476
00:39:49.253 --> 00:39:50.459
Absolutely.

477
00:39:51.155 --> 00:39:53.829
You don't even like me running,
and she is crazy about it.

478
00:39:53.924 --> 00:39:55.267
Look at this.

479
00:39:56.627 --> 00:39:58.106
Look at me.

480
00:39:58.963 --> 00:39:59.907
One second...

481
00:40:00.664 --> 00:40:02.871
- What are you doing?
- This is how it's done abroad.

482
00:40:03.334 --> 00:40:06.406
Stupid girl!
Abroad, what they do is...

483
00:40:06.504 --> 00:40:09.451
here... right here
and then...

484
00:40:12.309 --> 00:40:14.118
This is the moment...

485
00:40:15.579 --> 00:40:17.581
to show your valour...

486
00:40:19.350 --> 00:40:23.025
and die for your country
which is every soldier's dream.

487
00:40:23.854 --> 00:40:25.162
Soldiers...

488
00:40:25.856 --> 00:40:29.030
you have undergone
rigorous training...

489
00:40:29.593 --> 00:40:32.039
and now it's time to
show your strength.

490
00:40:33.964 --> 00:40:37.434
They have started the war
but we will end it!

491
00:40:39.336 --> 00:40:41.839
Promise your motherland that...

492
00:40:42.640 --> 00:40:47.020
before you become a martyr,
you will kill ten of the enemy!

493
00:40:49.447 --> 00:40:51.449
- 51...
- Victory!

494
00:40:51.549 --> 00:40:53.324
- 51...
- Victory!

495
00:40:53.417 --> 00:40:55.363
- 51...
- Victory!

496
00:41:20.845 --> 00:41:22.756
- The code will be Bravo.
- Yes, sir.

497
00:41:22.847 --> 00:41:25.259
- G.S reservation.
- Yes, sir.

498
00:41:25.349 --> 00:41:27.386
The Battalion moves at 1500 hours.

499
00:41:27.485 --> 00:41:28.259
- Any doubt?
- No, sir.

500
00:41:28.385 --> 00:41:29.295
Move.

501
00:41:29.787 --> 00:41:30.891
Victory to India.

502
00:41:32.556 --> 00:41:33.694
Sir.

503
00:41:33.991 --> 00:41:35.732
Paan Singh... at ease.

504
00:41:36.160 --> 00:41:37.468
Yes?

505
00:41:37.561 --> 00:41:39.871
Sir, why can't I
go to the battlefront?

506
00:41:39.964 --> 00:41:43.502
It's an Army rule.
Athletes are not sent to the front.

507
00:41:44.568 --> 00:41:46.411
I have a point...

508
00:41:47.605 --> 00:41:50.745
I won't be able to face my people
in the village...

509
00:41:51.141 --> 00:41:54.384
Sir, please!
The army can take all my medals...

510
00:41:54.478 --> 00:41:58.483
I'm ready to fore go sports.
I cannot lose this opportunity.

511
00:41:58.582 --> 00:42:01.688
Let me go there once, please.

512
00:42:01.785 --> 00:42:03.321
You will stay right here.

513
00:42:05.022 --> 00:42:06.262
Move.

514
00:42:20.037 --> 00:42:22.779
What happened, Paan Singh?
Not coming to the front?

515
00:42:23.207 --> 00:42:24.584
On sick leave?

516
00:42:32.616 --> 00:42:34.926
- 51...
- Victory!

517
00:42:35.019 --> 00:42:37.226
- 51...
- Victory!

518
00:42:43.193 --> 00:42:46.766
The war of 1965 took place
and they said...

519
00:42:47.565 --> 00:42:49.545
athletes are the nation's
precious treasure.

520
00:42:49.633 --> 00:42:51.772
And they won't be sent to war.

521
00:42:51.869 --> 00:42:54.713
I desperately wished
I could do away with the rule.

522
00:42:55.339 --> 00:42:58.548
My wish of defeating the enemy
did not die out...

523
00:42:59.176 --> 00:43:00.780
and I got my chance.

524
00:43:00.878 --> 00:43:02.380
In the year 1967.

525
00:43:02.980 --> 00:43:05.392
At the International Defense Meet.

526
00:43:06.383 --> 00:43:08.021
He's lost it.
Sir, explain it to him.

527
00:43:08.118 --> 00:43:11.531
There are athletes half his age.
He'll definitely lose.

528
00:43:12.156 --> 00:43:14.136
It's impossible to
explain this to him.

529
00:43:14.224 --> 00:43:15.669
He wasn't able to fight in the war...

530
00:43:15.759 --> 00:43:18.103
so now, this is his battlefield.

531
00:43:18.195 --> 00:43:20.869
Sir, this is the International
Defense Athletic Meet...

532
00:43:20.965 --> 00:43:22.740
not a battlefield.

533
00:43:22.833 --> 00:43:24.335
For him it is!

534
00:43:27.004 --> 00:43:28.540
So, Paan Singh?

535
00:43:29.840 --> 00:43:32.184
You are participating in
an international meet.

536
00:43:33.477 --> 00:43:34.854
You've grown older.

537
00:43:36.246 --> 00:43:37.657
What if you lose?

538
00:43:38.916 --> 00:43:40.862
You didn't send me to
the battlefield...

539
00:43:40.951 --> 00:43:42.828
To put my life at stake

540
00:43:44.188 --> 00:43:47.431
Now with my self respect at stake, the
playground will be my battleground.

541
00:45:12.876 --> 00:45:16.756
That was the most
important race of my life.

542
00:45:17.314 --> 00:45:19.123
There was no record involved...

543
00:45:19.750 --> 00:45:21.286
- but that race...
- Excuse me?

544
00:45:21.385 --> 00:45:22.864
- Will you help me with this?
- Sure.

545
00:45:22.953 --> 00:45:24.330
The biggest race.

546
00:45:41.305 --> 00:45:44.650
Will you eat something?
The mutton looks delicious.

547
00:45:59.356 --> 00:46:02.667
Why did he eat it first?

548
00:46:02.960 --> 00:46:06.567
This is how my life is.
I need to be alert 24 hours.

549
00:46:07.397 --> 00:46:09.877
If it is poisoned,
the person who eats first, dies.

550
00:46:10.501 --> 00:46:11.070
Okay.

551
00:46:11.135 --> 00:46:12.978
The meat is absolutely delicious.

552
00:46:13.737 --> 00:46:15.978
Don't be shy, have some.

553
00:46:17.674 --> 00:46:18.846
Okay.

554
00:46:19.576 --> 00:46:23.183
Now I can proclaim
that I have dined with you.

555
00:46:26.416 --> 00:46:28.293
Let it be.
Meat is not good for you.

556
00:46:28.685 --> 00:46:30.722
Start running, lose some weight.

557
00:46:31.321 --> 00:46:33.130
- Then you can eat it.
- Right.

558
00:46:33.957 --> 00:46:35.834
Go on. I can continue talking.

559
00:46:37.027 --> 00:46:38.370
Okay.

560
00:46:44.234 --> 00:46:46.544
When did you leave the Army?

561
00:46:52.309 --> 00:46:55.882
In the recently concluded
International Defense Games...

562
00:46:55.946 --> 00:46:59.223
Subedaar Paan Singh Tomar,
broke his own record...

563
00:46:59.316 --> 00:47:03.992
in the 3000 meter steeplechase race,
to establish a brand new record.

564
00:47:04.087 --> 00:47:05.998
It means,
he broke his own record.

565
00:47:06.089 --> 00:47:06.897
Oh, okay.

566
00:47:06.990 --> 00:47:08.731
What's going on here?

567
00:47:11.829 --> 00:47:14.070
Now what is that
no-good brother of yours up to?

568
00:47:14.164 --> 00:47:15.973
What do you mean,
Bhanwar Singh?

569
00:47:16.066 --> 00:47:17.545
He's your cousin as well.

570
00:47:17.634 --> 00:47:19.204
So what has he done?

571
00:47:19.303 --> 00:47:22.250
Paan is the
national champion again.

572
00:47:22.339 --> 00:47:24.546
He's got a gold medal.

573
00:47:24.641 --> 00:47:27.815
A coward's job is to keep running.
What's the big deal?

574
00:47:27.911 --> 00:47:29.356
What are you saying?

575
00:47:29.446 --> 00:47:30.288
Why?

576
00:47:30.380 --> 00:47:32.826
He left his responsibilities,
and ran to the army.

577
00:47:32.916 --> 00:47:35.123
Let him come back.
I'll present him...

578
00:47:35.219 --> 00:47:37.199
with a gold medal.

579
00:47:37.287 --> 00:47:39.233
Stupid coward. Let's go.

580
00:47:42.392 --> 00:47:43.370
Father...

581
00:47:44.261 --> 00:47:45.763
father, uncle is here.

582
00:47:49.266 --> 00:47:51.746
He has grabbed the land
next to the well.

583
00:47:53.670 --> 00:47:55.650
They let animals loose
on standing crops.

584
00:47:57.007 --> 00:48:00.648
And when we protest
this is what happens.

585
00:48:02.279 --> 00:48:05.453
He has four licensed guns...
what can we do?

586
00:48:05.549 --> 00:48:08.052
Let's shoot Bhanwar Singh.
End of story.

587
00:48:08.151 --> 00:48:09.391
Shut up!

588
00:48:11.555 --> 00:48:13.660
You aren't even as heavy
as the gun...

589
00:48:19.863 --> 00:48:21.774
I can't handle this on my own.

590
00:48:22.666 --> 00:48:24.168
We have to do something.

591
00:48:34.478 --> 00:48:36.151
You are still the same.

592
00:48:36.713 --> 00:48:39.387
I'll be back in six months.
Fix your jumping.

593
00:48:39.483 --> 00:48:41.429
Don't ever let your regiment down.

594
00:48:41.685 --> 00:48:44.598
We will break the record
of your record-breaker.

595
00:48:44.721 --> 00:48:46.200
That's the spirit!

596
00:48:46.290 --> 00:48:48.930
- Victory to India.
- Subedaar...

597
00:48:50.027 --> 00:48:51.973
Colonel Masand is on line
from Gwalior.

598
00:48:59.670 --> 00:49:03.015
Sir, I've taken premature retirement.

599
00:49:03.106 --> 00:49:05.382
Are you going to quit the game?

600
00:49:05.943 --> 00:49:10.824
Household duties and farming,
are more dangerous sports.

601
00:49:11.114 --> 00:49:14.288
The coaching offer remains
open for you.

602
00:49:14.384 --> 00:49:15.294
Sorry?

603
00:49:15.385 --> 00:49:17.228
You can be a coach with the Army.

604
00:49:17.321 --> 00:49:18.231
Yes, sir.

605
00:49:18.322 --> 00:49:19.767
I want to give you something.

606
00:49:19.890 --> 00:49:22.700
You've helped my son become
an Army man. What else can I ask for?

607
00:49:22.759 --> 00:49:25.103
Colonel Masand
has sent this for you.

608
00:49:25.462 --> 00:49:28.102
It's ice cream. Rings a bell?

609
00:49:28.565 --> 00:49:31.478
Let's see, if it melts...

610
00:49:31.568 --> 00:49:33.514
by the time you reach home.

611
00:49:48.719 --> 00:49:50.721
This is my biggest medal, sir.

612
00:50:47.144 --> 00:50:48.452
Brother...

613
00:50:49.513 --> 00:50:50.821
Brother...

614
00:50:52.082 --> 00:50:53.390
- Let's go...
- What's the matter?

615
00:50:53.483 --> 00:50:55.190
Our fields have been...
Lets go.

616
00:50:55.285 --> 00:50:56.821
What happened...

617
00:50:57.320 --> 00:51:00.597
I was there last evening.
Everything was fine.

618
00:51:00.724 --> 00:51:03.102
Are you sure they are responsible?

619
00:51:04.161 --> 00:51:06.141
See here it is...

620
00:51:10.267 --> 00:51:11.541
Brother...

621
00:51:12.836 --> 00:51:14.076
Brother...

622
00:51:17.107 --> 00:51:19.246
What's the problem?

623
00:51:20.243 --> 00:51:21.654
What is it?

624
00:51:21.878 --> 00:51:23.084
Why are you barking
early in the morning?

625
00:51:23.180 --> 00:51:24.853
What is this?

626
00:51:24.948 --> 00:51:26.757
We own the farm,
worked hard on this crop.

627
00:51:26.850 --> 00:51:28.420
How can you cut it?

628
00:51:28.518 --> 00:51:29.895
This is stealing.

629
00:51:29.986 --> 00:51:31.863
Who made you the constable?

630
00:51:33.356 --> 00:51:34.858
Answer me!

631
00:51:35.459 --> 00:51:38.668
The field and crops belong to us.

632
00:51:38.762 --> 00:51:41.368
It's ours to burn at the
festival in two weeks.

633
00:51:41.598 --> 00:51:43.703
You can approach the court,
if you want to. Go!

634
00:51:43.800 --> 00:51:48.010
The courts are a pain
and no one benefits.

635
00:51:48.738 --> 00:51:51.719
This is our crop,
please give it back.

636
00:51:51.975 --> 00:51:54.854
But the documents show
this is our land.

637
00:51:55.045 --> 00:51:57.082
I have paid Matadin for it.

638
00:51:57.180 --> 00:51:59.160
Yes, he sold his share.

639
00:52:04.321 --> 00:52:07.393
Yes, he sold his share
but this is from my share.

640
00:52:07.624 --> 00:52:09.467
The land was divided equally
by the village council.

641
00:52:09.559 --> 00:52:11.061
That's funny!

642
00:52:12.195 --> 00:52:13.674
Listen, little boy...

643
00:52:14.231 --> 00:52:17.269
go and look at the
land records for yourself.

644
00:52:17.767 --> 00:52:20.941
Go to the council, or the court,
don't bother me.

645
00:52:21.171 --> 00:52:24.812
If I get angry,
Your fate will be decided right here

646
00:52:25.475 --> 00:52:26.852
What will you do?

647
00:52:28.145 --> 00:52:31.217
- Tell me...
- Paan Singh... let's go.

648
00:52:32.182 --> 00:52:33.684
What will you do?

649
00:52:36.419 --> 00:52:39.195
Let's go. Goodbye brother.

650
00:52:39.289 --> 00:52:42.600
Don't scare me with these guns...
I've seen bigger ones.

651
00:53:00.810 --> 00:53:02.721
Colonel Masand?

652
00:53:03.547 --> 00:53:04.753
Jai Hind, sir.

653
00:53:05.215 --> 00:53:07.195
Subedaar Paan Singh speaking.

654
00:53:09.619 --> 00:53:12.930
I'm in trouble.
Things aren't good.

655
00:53:13.290 --> 00:53:16.328
My relatives have
seized my farm and land.

656
00:53:16.426 --> 00:53:18.406
It's been two years now.

657
00:53:18.962 --> 00:53:20.168
Can your brother...

658
00:53:20.263 --> 00:53:22.800
request the Collector of
Morena to solve our case?

659
00:53:22.933 --> 00:53:24.640
He's lying, sir.

660
00:53:25.068 --> 00:53:28.015
We own the land.
They only till the land.

661
00:53:28.104 --> 00:53:30.914
This document will prove
who is lying.

662
00:53:31.007 --> 00:53:34.284
My brother has sold his land,
I've have not sold mine.

663
00:53:34.377 --> 00:53:38.848
They've bribed their way
to register the land in their name.

664
00:53:38.982 --> 00:53:40.393
This is our land.

665
00:53:40.483 --> 00:53:42.588
Aren't you related?

666
00:53:42.686 --> 00:53:44.962
Yes, we are cousins...

667
00:53:45.288 --> 00:53:47.199
that's why he is alive.

668
00:53:47.290 --> 00:53:49.793
That is why you're alive, uncle...

669
00:53:49.893 --> 00:53:52.737
I wish I could celebrate
your death anniversary.

670
00:53:52.829 --> 00:53:55.435
Shut up!
Not in front of the collector.

671
00:53:56.099 --> 00:53:57.134
Look...

672
00:53:57.234 --> 00:53:58.679
Hanumanta is here.

673
00:53:59.769 --> 00:54:01.510
He got leave.

674
00:54:05.041 --> 00:54:06.281
Greetings, father.

675
00:54:06.376 --> 00:54:08.049
The Bhanwar Singh dispute
is still on?

676
00:54:08.144 --> 00:54:10.556
The Collector is here to sort it out.

677
00:54:10.647 --> 00:54:12.251
Calm down, Hanumanta.

678
00:54:12.349 --> 00:54:15.125
The country needs you.

679
00:54:15.218 --> 00:54:17.289
Don't die for such petty issues.

680
00:54:17.387 --> 00:54:19.424
Shut up, will you!

681
00:54:19.656 --> 00:54:21.932
Respect the Collector.

682
00:54:23.226 --> 00:54:24.534
Bhanwar Singh...

683
00:54:25.228 --> 00:54:28.971
the papers prove
Paan Singh's ownership

684
00:54:29.065 --> 00:54:30.271
on the land.

685
00:54:31.301 --> 00:54:33.577
You own enough land...

686
00:54:33.670 --> 00:54:35.980
stop fighting over such small issues.

687
00:54:36.072 --> 00:54:38.484
Solve this amicably.

688
00:54:38.575 --> 00:54:40.020
Sir...

689
00:54:40.076 --> 00:54:41.146
Sir...

690
00:54:41.278 --> 00:54:45.556
Sir, their family owns
seven licensed guns...

691
00:54:45.649 --> 00:54:47.151
which they threaten us with.

692
00:54:47.250 --> 00:54:50.720
Please confiscate them
till this problem is solved.

693
00:54:50.820 --> 00:54:53.699
I came here on Masand's request...

694
00:54:53.790 --> 00:54:57.636
but you have to resolve
it amongst yourselves.

695
00:54:57.727 --> 00:54:59.673
You have the authority.

696
00:54:59.763 --> 00:55:01.606
They keep threatening us
with their guns.

697
00:55:01.698 --> 00:55:03.234
An army man petrified by a gun!

698
00:55:03.333 --> 00:55:04.744
Let's fight without weapons then.

699
00:55:04.801 --> 00:55:08.112
This is the aggression of
Chambal Valley. Solve it yourselves!

700
00:55:09.172 --> 00:55:12.119
Following your
father's footsteps... are you?

701
00:55:12.742 --> 00:55:14.346
Your father never fought in a war.

702
00:55:14.444 --> 00:55:17.220
Since you're spoiling for a fight,
listen to this.

703
00:55:17.314 --> 00:55:19.260
We have such a huge family that...

704
00:55:19.349 --> 00:55:22.262
we can drown you in our urine.

705
00:55:22.352 --> 00:55:24.195
Mind your language, uncle.

706
00:55:24.287 --> 00:55:25.732
Let's leave, Paan.

707
00:55:39.135 --> 00:55:40.512
Burn it all..

708
00:55:44.841 --> 00:55:47.947
It's Paan Singh's crop.
Burn it.

709
00:55:49.045 --> 00:55:51.150
Yes, keep burning.

710
00:56:16.840 --> 00:56:18.842
I won't spare anything, damned.

711
00:56:18.908 --> 00:56:20.751
Not a single grain

712
00:56:48.304 --> 00:56:49.783
You bastard!

713
00:56:57.013 --> 00:56:59.687
Where are you going?

714
00:57:03.219 --> 00:57:08.601
Why are we exerting ourselves.
Just shoot him!

715
00:57:08.925 --> 00:57:10.165
Let him go.

716
00:57:10.226 --> 00:57:12.638
Let him go?
And what about his father?

717
00:57:12.729 --> 00:57:14.800
He can do nothing.

718
00:57:16.232 --> 00:57:19.441
But run to the police.

719
00:57:20.170 --> 00:57:22.650
That's all he can do.

720
00:57:22.739 --> 00:57:23.979
Run.

721
00:57:25.008 --> 00:57:27.420
If he had any guts...

722
00:57:27.510 --> 00:57:30.116
he'd have used the gun by now.

723
00:57:32.115 --> 00:57:34.595
Tomorrow, we shall get them all.

724
00:57:35.718 --> 00:57:37.720
Let the whole village know
who's boss.

725
00:57:40.457 --> 00:57:41.697
Who is that?

726
00:57:41.791 --> 00:57:43.862
Over there... who is that?

727
00:57:53.770 --> 00:57:55.374
Don't stop me today, father.

728
00:57:55.472 --> 00:57:56.473
Let me go.

729
00:57:58.675 --> 00:58:00.177
You don't have the courage...

730
00:58:00.276 --> 00:58:01.755
to resolve this farce.

731
00:58:02.545 --> 00:58:04.684
I will settle this
with Bhanwar Singh.

732
00:58:04.781 --> 00:58:07.728
Put down your guns.
Violence won't solve anything.

733
00:58:08.852 --> 00:58:11.389
It will not heal my son's wounds...

734
00:58:11.488 --> 00:58:14.230
What about our honor?
Our pride?

735
00:58:14.290 --> 00:58:17.863
What about it?
We won't shed more blood.

736
00:58:18.528 --> 00:58:20.667
My son is an Army man.

737
00:58:21.297 --> 00:58:24.608
The Army considers
me a national treasure.

738
00:58:25.268 --> 00:58:26.872
Won't the police listen to me?

739
00:58:37.447 --> 00:58:40.656
What's the proof that this is you?

740
00:58:42.218 --> 00:58:43.458
And what is this...

741
00:58:44.153 --> 00:58:46.155
Steeple... chase.

742
00:58:46.689 --> 00:58:49.169
- Chase?
- Yes, sir.

743
00:58:49.292 --> 00:58:51.465
So, who chases whom?

744
00:58:51.561 --> 00:58:53.632
There is no chase here, sir.

745
00:58:53.730 --> 00:58:57.473
This is a hurdle race,
3000 meters long.

746
00:58:57.534 --> 00:58:59.207
One has to jump
across barriers...

747
00:58:59.302 --> 00:59:01.646
It is the most grueling race.

748
00:59:06.175 --> 00:59:07.620
How do we know it's you?

749
00:59:07.710 --> 00:59:09.087
Here is the proof, sir.

750
00:59:09.145 --> 00:59:10.715
This is me.

751
00:59:10.813 --> 00:59:12.087
This is me.

752
00:59:12.749 --> 00:59:14.057
This is also me.

753
00:59:20.089 --> 00:59:21.932
You were young then.

754
00:59:25.662 --> 00:59:29.633
Why do people abroad
wear such skimpy clothes?

755
00:59:29.999 --> 00:59:31.376
Well...

756
00:59:31.467 --> 00:59:33.970
You must have feast your eyes!

757
00:59:34.070 --> 00:59:35.879
How did you travel?

758
00:59:35.972 --> 00:59:38.646
By air, or by ship?

759
00:59:38.741 --> 00:59:42.279
This is no time for discussion.
My son's life is in danger.

760
00:59:42.345 --> 00:59:45.554
I've won medals for the country.

761
00:59:45.648 --> 00:59:47.252
I've been the national champion.

762
00:59:48.618 --> 00:59:50.757
I've been in the forces,
just like you.

763
00:59:51.354 --> 00:59:54.927
Neither the council nor the registrar
is hearing my case.

764
00:59:55.024 --> 00:59:56.264
Where do I go now?

765
00:59:56.359 --> 01:00:00.330
Listen, this is a
land and family dispute.

766
01:00:00.830 --> 01:00:04.300
Without a few dead bodies,
how can we intervene?

767
01:00:04.400 --> 01:00:07.347
- What I'm trying to say...
- This is Morena district...

768
01:00:07.403 --> 01:00:09.144
the police is revered here.

769
01:00:09.272 --> 01:00:10.342
I'm saying...

770
01:00:10.406 --> 01:00:13.649
What will people say
if we meddle in petty issues?

771
01:00:13.743 --> 01:00:15.780
I'm not asking you to
solve the land dispute.

772
01:00:15.878 --> 01:00:18.415
But they thrashed
my son mercilessly...

773
01:00:18.514 --> 01:00:20.551
within an inch of his life.

774
01:00:20.650 --> 01:00:21.754
He can't move...

775
01:00:21.851 --> 01:00:23.888
But he's breathing, isn't he?

776
01:00:25.888 --> 01:00:27.697
He isn't dead yet.

777
01:00:27.790 --> 01:00:30.930
Should I wait till he dies?

778
01:00:31.027 --> 01:00:32.335
I have run for my
country in vain!

779
01:00:32.428 --> 01:00:34.533
But you got your medals.

780
01:00:36.032 --> 01:00:37.409
Now get out of here.

781
01:00:37.500 --> 01:00:38.604
Get lost.

782
01:00:38.701 --> 01:00:39.873
Get lost.

783
01:01:06.462 --> 01:01:08.533
Your duty is to protect people.

784
01:01:08.631 --> 01:01:09.769
So?

785
01:01:09.866 --> 01:01:11.573
Not to feast on their blood.

786
01:01:12.335 --> 01:01:14.008
What... what did you say?

787
01:01:14.837 --> 01:01:17.010
You heard it.

788
01:01:17.373 --> 01:01:19.011
Don't act like you can't hear me.

789
01:01:19.108 --> 01:01:21.486
You've got corruption written
all over you!

790
01:01:22.345 --> 01:01:25.622
A pimp would do your job better.

791
01:01:25.715 --> 01:01:28.321
- You bloody two-cent of a soldier.
- Son of a bitch!

792
01:01:28.418 --> 01:01:30.056
Stop your crap... and get out.

793
01:01:30.153 --> 01:01:33.965
Do you want to be beaten up?

794
01:01:34.057 --> 01:01:37.937
I'll beat the life out of you!

795
01:01:38.027 --> 01:01:41.133
I'll rip that uniform off you.
Bloody pimp!

796
01:01:41.230 --> 01:01:42.800
Get lost!

797
01:01:56.846 --> 01:01:59.383
Where is he?
Tell him to come with the guns.

798
01:02:00.283 --> 01:02:02.285
There will be a river of blood today.

799
01:02:02.385 --> 01:02:06.299
You are relaxing here and
Paan Singh's gone to file a complaint.

800
01:02:06.422 --> 01:02:09.403
He's a stubborn man.
We have to get rid of him.

801
01:02:09.492 --> 01:02:12.439
If he were a real man, he
wouldn't keep running to the police.

802
01:02:17.467 --> 01:02:20.539
Beware, there'll be violence today.

803
01:02:23.773 --> 01:02:25.719
Bhanwar Singh is coming...

804
01:02:26.309 --> 01:02:28.255
Run...
Bhanwar Singh is here.

805
01:02:28.377 --> 01:02:32.416
With his cronies...
and they have guns.

806
01:02:32.482 --> 01:02:37.329
These bastards need...
to be taught a lesson.

807
01:02:37.453 --> 01:02:40.434
Do we have no pride that
anyone can walk in when father is out?

808
01:02:40.523 --> 01:02:41.524
Please don't go there.

809
01:02:41.624 --> 01:02:43.035
Wait, don't go.
- What's wrong?

810
01:02:43.126 --> 01:02:45.003
Where are you going with that gun?

811
01:02:45.094 --> 01:02:46.869
Mother... mother... hide.

812
01:02:57.073 --> 01:02:58.108
They are coming!

813
01:02:58.207 --> 01:02:59.652
Why did you have to shoot?

814
01:02:59.742 --> 01:03:00.880
Run to the roof.

815
01:03:01.210 --> 01:03:02.120
Break the door!

816
01:03:02.211 --> 01:03:04.885
- Mother... hurry...
- You go, Bhanwar Singh won't hurt me.

817
01:03:06.849 --> 01:03:08.795
Come on, Bhanwar Singh!
I'll teach you!

818
01:03:08.851 --> 01:03:11.889
Break it down before they run!

819
01:03:12.789 --> 01:03:13.961
Break it!

820
01:03:20.163 --> 01:03:21.574
Jump!

821
01:03:24.033 --> 01:03:26.035
Mother, this way...

822
01:03:26.335 --> 01:03:27.006
Run!

823
01:03:29.071 --> 01:03:32.109
What do you think you're doing?

824
01:03:32.208 --> 01:03:34.051
Have some respect.

825
01:03:34.143 --> 01:03:35.952
Get out of my house now!

826
01:03:40.616 --> 01:03:42.721
Old woman, where's your son now?!

827
01:03:42.819 --> 01:03:44.856
Help.. help..

828
01:03:54.130 --> 01:03:55.575
It's a bad time.

829
01:03:55.731 --> 01:03:58.405
We need ward off the evil eye.

830
01:03:59.168 --> 01:04:01.170
We need to make offerings.

831
01:04:01.270 --> 01:04:03.216
And arrange a prayer in the village.

832
01:04:03.306 --> 01:04:05.286
Subedaar, don't go home.

833
01:04:05.408 --> 01:04:07.649
Bhanwar Singh and his family
have attacked the house.

834
01:04:07.743 --> 01:04:08.813
There are bullets all over.

835
01:04:08.911 --> 01:04:10.618
The house is destroyed!

836
01:04:10.713 --> 01:04:12.420
They did not even spare mother.

837
01:04:12.882 --> 01:04:14.953
They are on the look out for you.

838
01:04:15.051 --> 01:04:15.961
Where is my son?

839
01:04:16.052 --> 01:04:18.498
Your wife has taken the
kids to her mother's village.

840
01:04:18.821 --> 01:04:20.129
Is there anyone at home?

841
01:04:20.223 --> 01:04:21.497
No one.

842
01:04:37.406 --> 01:04:40.910
Mother asked me to
give these bangles to you.

843
01:04:56.659 --> 01:04:59.799
Mother, till things cool down...

844
01:05:00.463 --> 01:05:02.136
we'll live here.

845
01:05:02.865 --> 01:05:04.776
Jairaj...

846
01:05:05.268 --> 01:05:06.941
- Where are you going with the gun?
- I'm not going anywhere!

847
01:05:07.036 --> 01:05:09.448
Come back, I say!

848
01:05:09.538 --> 01:05:11.074
I'll be here.

849
01:05:11.874 --> 01:05:13.478
Look father is here.

850
01:05:21.450 --> 01:05:23.088
What do we do now?

851
01:05:24.320 --> 01:05:26.163
If we go back to the village
we'll be killed.

852
01:05:26.822 --> 01:05:28.733
The police don't care.

853
01:05:30.293 --> 01:05:32.899
Will you lead the rest
of your life at your in-laws'?

854
01:05:32.995 --> 01:05:34.997
We have to get back to the village...

855
01:05:35.097 --> 01:05:37.008
and the police better care.

856
01:05:39.101 --> 01:05:41.741
Hanumanta, you get back
to duty tomorrow.

857
01:05:41.871 --> 01:05:42.815
I will not go back.

858
01:05:42.905 --> 01:05:43.975
Shut up!

859
01:05:45.942 --> 01:05:48.445
Your life has just started, son.

860
01:05:48.544 --> 01:05:50.649
I've lived mine already.

861
01:05:51.080 --> 01:05:53.492
You will join your unit tomorrow.
Say 'yes'.

862
01:05:55.384 --> 01:05:56.624
Yes.

863
01:05:57.853 --> 01:06:00.026
What about our unit, uncle?

864
01:06:00.122 --> 01:06:01.362
Our unit?

865
01:06:11.834 --> 01:06:14.371
Our unit leaves
tomorrow morning.

866
01:06:31.921 --> 01:06:33.457
Take care of yourself.

867
01:07:38.256 --> 01:07:39.530
Move it...

868
01:07:51.569 --> 01:07:55.016
Mother's calling you,
she is not well.

869
01:07:55.406 --> 01:07:56.783
Alright.

870
01:08:07.952 --> 01:08:10.057
They shot my son...

871
01:08:14.325 --> 01:08:20.037
Run... -Where is Jigesh?
- He has gone to his parent's place.

872
01:08:20.064 --> 01:08:23.204
I've been telling him...
The cops will make your life hell!

873
01:08:23.268 --> 01:08:28.081
Listen everyone! -Let's go, brother.
- This is Paan Singh Tomar's gang.

874
01:08:28.139 --> 01:08:30.642
I haven't settled my scores yet...

875
01:08:30.742 --> 01:08:34.713
and I won't rest till I do.
I will be back.

876
01:08:35.013 --> 01:08:39.223
Bhanwar Singh,
now the game has started.

877
01:08:42.220 --> 01:08:44.166
Why are you talking like this?

878
01:08:44.822 --> 01:08:47.496
Surrender! Serve your sentence
and start coaching.

879
01:08:49.994 --> 01:08:53.806
I'm ready to come back
but if I leave...

880
01:08:54.065 --> 01:08:57.535
my family and relatives...
no one will be spared.

881
01:08:59.270 --> 01:09:03.810
God and you know
how much the game means to me.

882
01:09:04.175 --> 01:09:07.122
These cops and village council...
what do they know?!

883
01:09:07.245 --> 01:09:10.454
They have created another rebel
to run in the ravines.

884
01:09:14.652 --> 01:09:18.998
These are my nephews...
they're innocent, sir.

885
01:09:19.524 --> 01:09:22.095
Would you enlist them in the army...

886
01:09:22.193 --> 01:09:23.900
Why don't you
enlist them in your gang?

887
01:09:23.995 --> 01:09:26.100
No one is a rebel by choice.

888
01:09:26.197 --> 01:09:28.108
You and I will never meet again.

889
01:09:34.272 --> 01:09:36.274
My news will keep reaching you.

890
01:09:38.076 --> 01:09:40.852
Matadin is a pious fellow...

891
01:09:40.945 --> 01:09:43.357
he can't kill a fly
let alone commit a murder.

892
01:09:43.448 --> 01:09:45.155
Bloody bastards...

893
01:09:45.783 --> 01:09:48.730
Sir, listen to me...

894
01:09:48.820 --> 01:09:52.267
I wasn't there at all.
It's a lie.

895
01:09:52.357 --> 01:09:54.837
- Look.
- Inspector, please hear me out.

896
01:09:54.892 --> 01:09:58.806
I'll let you go...
on one condition.

897
01:09:58.896 --> 01:10:01.968
Tell me where I can find Paan Singh.

898
01:10:02.066 --> 01:10:03.773
I swear, I have no idea.

899
01:10:03.868 --> 01:10:05.279
They're lying!

900
01:10:05.370 --> 01:10:08.249
They will not answer easily.
Make them sit on the stick

901
01:10:08.306 --> 01:10:11.150
and they will start to sing

902
01:10:11.242 --> 01:10:12.744
Take them away!

903
01:10:12.810 --> 01:10:14.812
I'm asking for the last time.

904
01:10:14.879 --> 01:10:17.155
Where is Paan Singh?

905
01:10:17.515 --> 01:10:19.893
Don't spare them!

906
01:10:24.322 --> 01:10:27.531
What can we say...
things are very difficult.

907
01:10:27.592 --> 01:10:30.596
Bhanwar Singh has
made our lives miserable.

908
01:10:31.195 --> 01:10:35.200
The cops are questioning everyone
about your whereabouts.

909
01:10:35.299 --> 01:10:37.575
Where do we go now?

910
01:10:39.203 --> 01:10:42.013
I've arranged for
some police uniforms.

911
01:10:42.340 --> 01:10:46.516
When Subedaar was looking for you,
you were holidaying...

912
01:10:46.611 --> 01:10:49.649
now that the cops have beaten you up
you come whining.

913
01:10:49.714 --> 01:10:51.853
Why should he take you
into his gang?

914
01:10:51.949 --> 01:10:55.396
- Let us join your gang.
- Please...

915
01:10:55.486 --> 01:10:57.659
If you become a rebel you die.

916
01:10:57.722 --> 01:10:59.497
We're not living in any case.

917
01:11:07.532 --> 01:11:10.945
Have you tried this with ice cream?

918
01:11:11.035 --> 01:11:13.948
No, I haven't tasted
anything like that.

919
01:11:14.439 --> 01:11:16.441
Tastes like heaven!

920
01:11:22.413 --> 01:11:23.756
Here, have some.

921
01:11:23.815 --> 01:11:25.419
Come on!

922
01:11:34.659 --> 01:11:36.138
The bowl is for you.

923
01:11:39.397 --> 01:11:42.401
I've had ice cream in
many foreign countries...

924
01:11:43.034 --> 01:11:46.709
but the best is the German one.

925
01:11:48.539 --> 01:11:50.382
One in six different colours.

926
01:11:51.342 --> 01:11:56.087
And another one... you press a button
and the ice cream flows out like honey!

927
01:11:56.481 --> 01:11:57.721
Softy.

928
01:11:59.550 --> 01:12:01.291
You get it in Gwalior as well.

929
01:12:02.019 --> 01:12:03.828
Don't talk rubbish!

930
01:12:03.921 --> 01:12:07.130
No, no. You've come to the city
after a long time.

931
01:12:07.191 --> 01:12:08.727
You wouldn't know.

932
01:12:11.796 --> 01:12:14.174
Did all your relatives
join the gang?

933
01:12:14.232 --> 01:12:15.734
Bhanwar Singh filed complaints...

934
01:12:15.833 --> 01:12:17.710
against all of them
there was no other option.

935
01:12:21.906 --> 01:12:24.750
- How much is it for?
- What?

936
01:12:24.842 --> 01:12:27.482
- Softy.
- Two rupees fifty paise.

937
01:12:27.778 --> 01:12:28.950
How much?

938
01:12:29.046 --> 01:12:30.320
Two rupees fifty paise.

939
01:12:32.483 --> 01:12:33.655
Two...

940
01:12:39.023 --> 01:12:40.161
Where did you get your weapons from?

941
01:12:40.258 --> 01:12:41.794
We bought them, obviously.

942
01:12:42.159 --> 01:12:45.231
Your eyes are like
a double barrel gun...

943
01:12:45.329 --> 01:12:47.400
Your eyes are like
a double barrel gun...

944
01:12:47.498 --> 01:12:49.478
Your words are like
a double barrel gun...

945
01:12:49.534 --> 01:12:53.676
You give me a shock like a rifle...

946
01:13:02.113 --> 01:13:06.858
You're an expensive
weapon my darling...

947
01:13:06.951 --> 01:13:08.123
Come here...

948
01:13:10.421 --> 01:13:14.699
Happy Birthday to you...

949
01:13:14.792 --> 01:13:18.569
- Is singing all that she can do?
- Depends on how much money you have!

950
01:13:20.698 --> 01:13:22.041
Don't bother with this.

951
01:13:22.133 --> 01:13:26.445
It's not nearly enough.

952
01:13:27.705 --> 01:13:28.877
Go on...

953
01:13:33.911 --> 01:13:36.448
Keep it going,
I'll be back with the money.

954
01:13:48.359 --> 01:13:50.862
One move and I'll give
you a bullet for your birthday!

955
01:14:00.671 --> 01:14:04.619
Oh my, a garland of notes.

956
01:14:04.709 --> 01:14:06.655
Hey Balram, drop it.

957
01:14:06.744 --> 01:14:08.746
You're a rebel.
Stop acting like a fool.

958
01:14:08.813 --> 01:14:11.225
What will you
do with that cheap garland?

959
01:14:11.482 --> 01:14:13.086
Ramcharan, come here...

960
01:14:15.953 --> 01:14:17.660
Inform the boy's family...

961
01:14:20.024 --> 01:14:21.901
and ask them for a ransom of
125,000 rupees.

962
01:14:22.426 --> 01:14:24.235
And if they inform the cops...

963
01:14:25.563 --> 01:14:27.543
he will lose his life.

964
01:14:28.499 --> 01:14:29.671
Do you understand?

965
01:14:30.401 --> 01:14:31.641
Say, 'understood'.

966
01:14:33.771 --> 01:14:34.647
Brother...

967
01:14:35.773 --> 01:14:39.778
Ask Govardhan, the barber
to inform the boy's family.

968
01:14:39.844 --> 01:14:41.653
- Right now?
- Yes...

969
01:14:42.413 --> 01:14:43.915
You sit here, with me.

970
01:14:46.350 --> 01:14:49.627
- What are you doing?
- Making sure he doesn't run away.

971
01:14:51.155 --> 01:14:53.533
You think he can outrun me?

972
01:14:55.126 --> 01:14:56.469
Get him to work.

973
01:14:56.560 --> 01:14:59.700
There is no free lunch here
he will have to cook for the gang.

974
01:15:00.398 --> 01:15:01.775
So, tell me...

975
01:15:01.866 --> 01:15:04.608
I dealt the cards.
It's your turn to play.

976
01:15:04.702 --> 01:15:06.648
You call these cards?

977
01:15:07.605 --> 01:15:09.812
I just taught you how to deal.

978
01:15:10.141 --> 01:15:13.179
- I have a hand.
- You dealt a wrong hand.

979
01:15:27.625 --> 01:15:32.199
- Have you arranged the ransom?
- I have 75,000 rupees.

980
01:15:32.263 --> 01:15:38.407
-It's 125,000 to free the boy.
- But this is all I have.

981
01:15:39.136 --> 01:15:42.242
You better shed tears worth 50,000!

982
01:15:42.606 --> 01:15:46.713
If the Subedaar gets emotional,
your son might be freed.

983
01:15:46.777 --> 01:15:49.951
Everything depends on you.

984
01:15:55.286 --> 01:15:59.325
That's not good.
You need to cry a river!

985
01:16:14.138 --> 01:16:17.051
Make sure that the Subedaar
doesn't get annoyed...

986
01:16:17.541 --> 01:16:20.420
otherwise we aren't responsible
for your life.

987
01:16:21.145 --> 01:16:22.453
There he is.

988
01:16:24.515 --> 01:16:26.119
Subedaar...

989
01:16:29.153 --> 01:16:31.656
I couldn't arrange 125,000 rupees.

990
01:16:31.722 --> 01:16:34.896
I sold everything and
managed 75,000.

991
01:16:34.992 --> 01:16:37.063
You can check, if you want to.

992
01:16:37.161 --> 01:16:39.402
He is bargaining for his own son.

993
01:16:39.463 --> 01:16:42.034
Don't believe a word...
he is trying to dupe us.

994
01:16:42.099 --> 01:16:44.238
We are rebels, not businessmen...

995
01:16:44.301 --> 01:16:45.712
give us what you have and leave.

996
01:16:45.770 --> 01:16:48.944
- We'll release him in a week.
- In a week?

997
01:16:49.006 --> 01:16:50.917
Well, what if you turn informer?

998
01:16:50.975 --> 01:16:54.980
I don't have the grit
to inform the police.

999
01:16:55.079 --> 01:16:57.582
Count the money, before taking it.

1000
01:16:58.883 --> 01:17:00.021
Get away.

1001
01:17:05.689 --> 01:17:07.760
Shall I tell him, where we found you?

1002
01:17:10.060 --> 01:17:14.372
He was busy with a nautch girl.
We caught him then.

1003
01:17:14.732 --> 01:17:17.713
Superb! So you enjoy dancing girls...

1004
01:17:17.768 --> 01:17:21.944
while I go bankrupt
trying to save you.

1005
01:17:22.006 --> 01:17:23.451
Should I tell the Subedaar

1006
01:17:23.507 --> 01:17:25.009
about your misdeeds?

1007
01:17:25.109 --> 01:17:28.682
What about your mistress
who you send...

1008
01:17:28.779 --> 01:17:32.022
10,000 rupees to every month!
Shall ll:ell him...

1009
01:17:32.116 --> 01:17:35.529
Subedaar, kill the bugger.
You want to argue with me!

1010
01:17:35.619 --> 01:17:37.530
You didn't even bring
the entire ransom!

1011
01:17:37.588 --> 01:17:41.001
- I'm your bloody father.
- Bad excuse for a father.

1012
01:17:41.058 --> 01:17:43.231
Come here, boy.

1013
01:17:44.094 --> 01:17:45.801
Your tears won't help!

1014
01:17:45.896 --> 01:17:47.466
Wish you weren't my son!

1015
01:17:47.565 --> 01:17:49.044
Bring him here.

1016
01:17:49.099 --> 01:17:50.942
Subedaar, kill him.

1017
01:17:51.035 --> 01:17:53.777
- Move it!
- You can kill him.

1018
01:17:53.871 --> 01:17:56.249
You're playing games with me!

1019
01:17:56.307 --> 01:17:58.981
Your son is following
in your footsteps.

1020
01:17:59.076 --> 01:18:01.022
What an interesting family!

1021
01:18:01.612 --> 01:18:05.856
Now, pay up 75,000 for your son
and another 75,000 for your self.

1022
01:18:06.517 --> 01:18:09.930
Give me 150,000 and you can go.

1023
01:18:09.987 --> 01:18:11.591
But Subedaar...

1024
01:18:11.655 --> 01:18:15.967
If I decide to make you dance
you'll be damned!

1025
01:18:17.661 --> 01:18:19.140
Tie both of them up!

1026
01:18:19.196 --> 01:18:22.473
This rubbish is spoiling
the peace of the ravines.

1027
01:18:24.902 --> 01:18:30.443
We had an understanding
with the border police.

1028
01:18:30.908 --> 01:18:34.082
As long as we didn't
mess in their area...

1029
01:18:34.178 --> 01:18:36.124
they didn't trouble us.

1030
01:18:36.680 --> 01:18:40.321
We carried out so many kidnappings
in collusion with the police.

1031
01:18:40.417 --> 01:18:42.055
On their instructions!

1032
01:18:44.021 --> 01:18:50.495
Om Prakash, the cloth merchant
had lent me four thousand rupees.

1033
01:18:51.195 --> 01:18:54.199
But the interest exceeded the loan.

1034
01:18:55.065 --> 01:18:59.138
Sir, he's a big fish.
We should get hold of him.

1035
01:18:59.570 --> 01:19:02.346
My loan will get waived,
and you will also benefit.

1036
01:19:02.406 --> 01:19:05.046
Is this a plan
or an invitation from Death?

1037
01:19:05.109 --> 01:19:08.989
Sir, all I want is revenge.

1038
01:19:09.079 --> 01:19:12.390
Great! Your rivalry
and our funeral pyre!

1039
01:19:12.449 --> 01:19:14.395
Don't listen to him.

1040
01:19:14.551 --> 01:19:17.532
He's made plans
to get us killed in UP.

1041
01:19:18.422 --> 01:19:20.459
Our corpses will float in the Ganges.

1042
01:19:20.557 --> 01:19:22.298
Don't give us this nonsense.

1043
01:19:23.627 --> 01:19:26.506
Where is the full house
you were mentioning?

1044
01:19:27.097 --> 01:19:28.337
Here's my last card.

1045
01:19:29.433 --> 01:19:30.810
It's my set!

1046
01:19:32.970 --> 01:19:36.349
We need to get past
the police of three states.

1047
01:19:36.440 --> 01:19:39.512
Madhya Pradesh, Uttar Pradesh
and Rajasthan.

1048
01:19:39.610 --> 01:19:42.682
Exactly! He's got plans
to get us killed.

1049
01:19:42.746 --> 01:19:45.090
Leave Rajasthan to me.

1050
01:19:45.182 --> 01:19:48.925
You think the cops of
UP and MP will welcome us?

1051
01:19:51.355 --> 01:19:52.732
Arrange for a police jeep.

1052
01:19:52.756 --> 01:19:53.564
Done.

1053
01:19:53.624 --> 01:19:55.865
Who can drive well?

1054
01:19:55.926 --> 01:19:57.098
I can.

1055
01:20:03.567 --> 01:20:06.707
We are at the MP and Rajasthan border.
Hurry up and change.

1056
01:20:13.978 --> 01:20:15.548
Let them pass.

1057
01:21:04.628 --> 01:21:05.834
There are cops up ahead.

1058
01:21:05.929 --> 01:21:09.103
So what! We're officers.
Keep driving.

1059
01:21:22.046 --> 01:21:25.357
We've got a report,
you're sheltering rebels.

1060
01:21:25.916 --> 01:21:28.021
Inspector, someone's misinformed you.

1061
01:22:06.256 --> 01:22:08.258
You aren't the police.

1062
01:22:08.325 --> 01:22:10.134
Correct, better late than never.

1063
01:22:10.794 --> 01:22:14.799
My name is Subedaar Paan Singh Tomar
and you have been kidnapped.

1064
01:22:14.865 --> 01:22:16.208
Say 'yes'.

1065
01:22:20.170 --> 01:22:22.878
You tricked the police
of three states.

1066
01:22:23.740 --> 01:22:25.344
Must have created quite a scandal.

1067
01:22:27.311 --> 01:22:29.052
That's the pity!

1068
01:22:30.114 --> 01:22:34.585
I crossed 28 barriers and 7 water pits
to become the national champion...

1069
01:22:34.685 --> 01:22:35.925
Nobody cared.

1070
01:22:37.721 --> 01:22:40.759
But when I became a kidnapper
and fooled the police...

1071
01:22:40.824 --> 01:22:43.498
everybody started chanting,
Paan Singh... Paan Singh

1072
01:22:44.061 --> 01:22:45.335
I agree.

1073
01:22:46.797 --> 01:22:48.208
Sports persons are not treated well.

1074
01:22:48.298 --> 01:22:50.278
Stop shedding crocodile tears.

1075
01:22:50.934 --> 01:22:52.811
If I was just an athlete...

1076
01:22:52.870 --> 01:22:55.043
would you have risked so much
to interview me?

1077
01:22:56.373 --> 01:22:57.511
You are right.

1078
01:23:01.378 --> 01:23:04.086
Is it true you got 400,000 rupees...

1079
01:23:04.181 --> 01:23:05.626
for the Om Prakash kidnapping?

1080
01:23:08.051 --> 01:23:10.554
And then we became
a complete gang.

1081
01:23:16.293 --> 01:23:18.500
Look at this one, brother.
I'm buying you a gun...

1082
01:23:20.797 --> 01:23:23.368
- put this there.
- Not this...it's for my prayers.

1083
01:23:23.467 --> 01:23:26.346
- Go, keep this there.
- Where?

1084
01:23:26.436 --> 01:23:27.881
There on the hillock.

1085
01:23:31.575 --> 01:23:32.986
If I need something else?

1086
01:23:34.077 --> 01:23:39.390
You'll get everything. Guns,
rifles, grenades, LMG, everything.

1087
01:23:39.449 --> 01:23:41.451
Put it there and move away.

1088
01:23:41.852 --> 01:23:44.458
- There, I've kept it.
- Okay, now move away!

1089
01:23:47.925 --> 01:23:50.166
Why are these guns numbered?

1090
01:23:52.996 --> 01:23:54.942
What's in a serial number?!

1091
01:23:56.633 --> 01:23:58.442
You have to keep
track of the material.

1092
01:24:00.737 --> 01:24:01.977
It's good, isn't it?

1093
01:24:03.507 --> 01:24:05.384
There are no criminals in the army.

1094
01:24:06.543 --> 01:24:08.648
This perhaps belonged to a policeman.

1095
01:24:09.746 --> 01:24:13.387
It doesn't matter where it comes from.
I just sell it.

1096
01:24:13.450 --> 01:24:14.554
Subedaar...

1097
01:24:16.453 --> 01:24:18.729
You are all over the radio.

1098
01:24:22.759 --> 01:24:24.102
Turn it off!

1099
01:24:27.097 --> 01:24:29.976
When I brought laurels for the country
nobody cared.

1100
01:24:30.033 --> 01:24:32.479
Now that I'm a rebel I'm famous!

1101
01:24:34.571 --> 01:24:36.050
Let me make this clear.

1102
01:24:38.675 --> 01:24:40.177
The bigger the gang...

1103
01:24:41.178 --> 01:24:42.714
the more the enemies.

1104
01:24:43.547 --> 01:24:45.322
Only two things can save us.

1105
01:24:45.916 --> 01:24:47.327
The first is...

1106
01:24:47.584 --> 01:24:49.427
our loyalty to each other.

1107
01:24:49.953 --> 01:24:51.830
And second, the support of our body.

1108
01:24:52.489 --> 01:24:54.833
Loyalty is our tradition.

1109
01:24:55.492 --> 01:24:57.472
And I'll train your bodies.

1110
01:24:58.228 --> 01:25:00.640
From tomorrow your military
training begins.

1111
01:25:01.565 --> 01:25:03.841
- Say, 'yes'.
- Yes.

1112
01:25:07.037 --> 01:25:08.072
Yes.

1113
01:25:09.039 --> 01:25:12.179
I can't tell the difference
between your yes and no.

1114
01:25:22.319 --> 01:25:23.992
Keep your head close to the ground.

1115
01:25:26.857 --> 01:25:30.100
A tortoise can easily win
a gold medal against you.

1116
01:25:30.661 --> 01:25:33.039
You resemble a bunch of goats
in a slaughter house.

1117
01:25:33.096 --> 01:25:34.507
Lift your gun higher!

1118
01:25:35.999 --> 01:25:38.741
Imagine there is constant fire
from here. You have to clear through.

1119
01:25:40.871 --> 01:25:42.942
So we need to learn
the scout formation.

1120
01:25:43.273 --> 01:25:47.050
In this formation
the first guy remains ahead...

1121
01:25:47.711 --> 01:25:51.488
while the second and fourth guys
are at an equal distance.

1122
01:25:52.215 --> 01:25:54.559
Nobody will come in each others way.

1123
01:26:06.330 --> 01:26:07.365
Keep sitting.

1124
01:26:12.903 --> 01:26:17.852
I can't do this, Paan.
Forgive me.

1125
01:26:18.909 --> 01:26:22.880
I'm not cut out for this.
If I keep at it I'll die too soon.

1126
01:26:22.946 --> 01:26:24.425
Fine, come and sit here.

1127
01:26:27.050 --> 01:26:29.656
Uncle, what is the
meaning of this parade?

1128
01:26:29.753 --> 01:26:31.494
While the enemy sleeps peacefully.

1129
01:26:32.089 --> 01:26:33.762
It's a temporary slumber...

1130
01:26:34.658 --> 01:26:36.001
What do you mean?

1131
01:26:36.093 --> 01:26:38.664
Very soon they
will be sleeping permanently.

1132
01:26:39.162 --> 01:26:40.641
How much more time?

1133
01:26:41.164 --> 01:26:44.338
We have our own gang, our weapons.

1134
01:26:45.669 --> 01:26:47.546
All you say is, There is time ...

1135
01:26:47.604 --> 01:26:49.345
it's not easy to attack them.

1136
01:26:49.406 --> 01:26:51.545
There are machine guns everywhere.

1137
01:26:51.608 --> 01:26:54.680
The house resembles a fort now
with constant patrolling.

1138
01:26:57.714 --> 01:27:01.059
The soil's getting damp.

1139
01:27:01.718 --> 01:27:06.360
Sowing begins in a few days...
and crops don't grow inside the house.

1140
01:27:07.824 --> 01:27:10.100
They'll all come to the fields.

1141
01:27:13.797 --> 01:27:16.209
Isn't there any alcohol here?

1142
01:27:16.299 --> 01:27:18.575
All bars are closed.
All across the district?

1143
01:27:18.668 --> 01:27:21.877
I could have bought it from the market
but there'd be a rampage.

1144
01:27:21.938 --> 01:27:24.418
One shouldn't drink in the day.

1145
01:27:24.508 --> 01:27:26.010
I don't need your lecture!

1146
01:27:34.217 --> 01:27:35.560
What was that?!

1147
01:27:46.696 --> 01:27:47.970
It's an attack.

1148
01:27:48.231 --> 01:27:49.574
Paan Singh is back.

1149
01:27:50.000 --> 01:27:51.206
Come on...

1150
01:27:51.301 --> 01:27:52.871
Run... run!

1151
01:27:59.943 --> 01:28:02.048
Who's gang is this?

1152
01:28:02.145 --> 01:28:04.921
This is Paan Singh's gang, Inspector.

1153
01:28:06.516 --> 01:28:08.189
All of you, stand in a line.

1154
01:28:10.520 --> 01:28:11.726
No... No...

1155
01:28:11.855 --> 01:28:14.426
Why not?
He filed the wrong reports.

1156
01:28:14.524 --> 01:28:16.800
- That's because...
- He protects Bhanwar Singh!

1157
01:28:16.893 --> 01:28:21.569
He filed a complaint
and I was only investigating it.

1158
01:28:21.631 --> 01:28:24.077
Inspector, you forgot your duty.

1159
01:28:24.134 --> 01:28:25.340
But I'm a rebel...

1160
01:28:25.435 --> 01:28:27.210
and I remember my duties.

1161
01:28:27.270 --> 01:28:30.274
You stand by justice, Subedaar.

1162
01:28:31.208 --> 01:28:33.449
I have two kids...

1163
01:28:33.510 --> 01:28:35.183
Kids?

1164
01:28:37.013 --> 01:28:38.356
Look...

1165
01:28:38.748 --> 01:28:40.523
This is your uniform...

1166
01:28:41.184 --> 01:28:42.754
and look at you.

1167
01:28:42.853 --> 01:28:46.198
You dare wear this uniform again...

1168
01:28:46.256 --> 01:28:48.896
and you'll die a dog's death.

1169
01:28:49.459 --> 01:28:51.461
You are not worthy of this uniform.

1170
01:28:52.596 --> 01:28:55.736
Apologize... to your uniform. Now!

1171
01:29:00.504 --> 01:29:01.881
Please forgive me.

1172
01:29:01.972 --> 01:29:03.315
Not me... the uniform.

1173
01:29:08.945 --> 01:29:13.758
Dear uniform...
please forgive me.

1174
01:29:13.850 --> 01:29:15.796
You are not worthy
of an apology either.

1175
01:29:15.886 --> 01:29:17.957
Now stand straight... stand up!

1176
01:29:21.057 --> 01:29:23.901
Run as fast as you can.

1177
01:29:27.597 --> 01:29:29.474
Where is Bhanwar Singh?

1178
01:29:33.870 --> 01:29:35.315
Here he is!

1179
01:29:42.913 --> 01:29:45.086
Where will you run to, Bhanwar Singh?

1180
01:30:24.154 --> 01:30:26.464
Where are you running off to?

1181
01:30:30.560 --> 01:30:32.506
Did you think
you could out run me.

1182
01:30:35.999 --> 01:30:37.273
Tell me!

1183
01:30:40.136 --> 01:30:42.673
Where are your bodyguards?

1184
01:30:43.340 --> 01:30:45.547
And your licensed guns?

1185
01:30:50.413 --> 01:30:51.915
So, tell me...

1186
01:30:52.882 --> 01:30:55.055
all we had was a
small piece of land...

1187
01:30:55.118 --> 01:30:56.654
and you had to go and occupy it?

1188
01:30:56.753 --> 01:30:58.130
Please forgive me.

1189
01:30:58.221 --> 01:31:00.258
Now how will you till the land?

1190
01:31:00.323 --> 01:31:03.133
You can take your land,
take mine too...

1191
01:31:03.226 --> 01:31:06.696
- Just let me go.
- You thrashed my son...

1192
01:31:07.297 --> 01:31:09.174
till he was almost dead.

1193
01:31:09.332 --> 01:31:11.209
He was beaten to pulp!

1194
01:31:16.906 --> 01:31:19.011
What was my mother's fault?

1195
01:31:19.075 --> 01:31:21.385
That you hit her
with the butt of a gun?

1196
01:31:23.513 --> 01:31:26.551
You beat my mother
with the butt of the gun!

1197
01:31:28.451 --> 01:31:30.021
Forgive me, please.

1198
01:31:34.791 --> 01:31:37.328
I won't die with this bullet.

1199
01:31:37.427 --> 01:31:40.101
Please have some mercy.

1200
01:31:40.163 --> 01:31:42.700
You think I don't
have enough bullets...

1201
01:31:42.799 --> 01:31:44.608
Or you think I can't aim?

1202
01:31:48.138 --> 01:31:50.140
You were my brother...

1203
01:31:50.206 --> 01:31:51.913
brother... my elder brother...

1204
01:31:52.542 --> 01:31:54.886
I was an international athlete...

1205
01:31:55.679 --> 01:31:56.783
Forgive me...

1206
01:31:56.880 --> 01:32:00.851
Tell me where I went wrong...

1207
01:32:00.917 --> 01:32:03.761
that you snatched
my playing field from me?

1208
01:32:05.955 --> 01:32:09.095
You forced this gun into my hands.

1209
01:32:09.259 --> 01:32:11.432
And now I'm running laps
in the ravines.

1210
01:32:15.031 --> 01:32:17.341
How will we settle this score?

1211
01:32:18.635 --> 01:32:21.309
I want my answers.

1212
01:32:26.643 --> 01:32:31.717
Please forgive me, Paan.
You are my brother.

1213
01:32:31.915 --> 01:32:33.394
Keep the gun away.

1214
01:32:36.753 --> 01:32:38.824
Please forgive me.

1215
01:32:41.057 --> 01:32:42.764
As a brother, forgive me.

1216
01:32:46.529 --> 01:32:48.304
I can run...

1217
01:32:49.165 --> 01:32:51.839
I've been running my whole life.

1218
01:32:53.336 --> 01:32:55.475
If that's fate, so be it.

1219
01:33:05.415 --> 01:33:07.417
Answer me before you go.

1220
01:33:08.051 --> 01:33:09.428
Answer me!

1221
01:33:15.258 --> 01:33:18.831
Why are you always in a hurry?

1222
01:33:20.563 --> 01:33:23.635
We were discussing
something important...

1223
01:33:24.834 --> 01:33:26.177
and you had to intervene.

1224
01:33:27.370 --> 01:33:30.374
Drop your gun... now.

1225
01:33:36.379 --> 01:33:40.657
I'll get my answers...
when we meet in the afterlife.

1226
01:33:40.750 --> 01:33:43.356
My questions are still unanswered.

1227
01:33:46.089 --> 01:33:48.433
I had my revenge.

1228
01:33:49.826 --> 01:33:53.205
But in the ravines, enmity runs deep.

1229
01:33:54.898 --> 01:33:57.003
And then one day something happened...

1230
01:33:57.367 --> 01:34:00.473
because of which
I am telling you my story.

1231
01:34:04.107 --> 01:34:08.351
Shut up!
Stop your ridiculous song.

1232
01:34:08.545 --> 01:34:11.992
The food better be spicy
or off with your tongue!

1233
01:34:12.081 --> 01:34:14.425
Then you will
be miming the song forever

1234
01:34:15.985 --> 01:34:19.262
Your trust is a great honor.

1235
01:34:19.322 --> 01:34:21.859
The arrangements here
are fantastic.

1236
01:34:21.958 --> 01:34:23.301
We have a big gang.

1237
01:34:23.359 --> 01:34:25.168
Whenever we pass by,
we will come here.

1238
01:34:25.228 --> 01:34:25.968
Keep this.

1239
01:34:26.029 --> 01:34:28.134
- I cannot keep it.
- Keep it.

1240
01:34:28.198 --> 01:34:29.836
We have a big gang.

1241
01:34:29.899 --> 01:34:31.810
I don't want to become
a burden on you.

1242
01:34:31.868 --> 01:34:34.212
What if you
stopped respecting us!?

1243
01:34:37.574 --> 01:34:42.455
The word is that the Morena and
Gwalior police is on the move.

1244
01:34:42.912 --> 01:34:43.982
It's dangerous.

1245
01:34:44.080 --> 01:34:47.960
We shall stay here
until things settle down.

1246
01:34:51.654 --> 01:34:53.531
Come and get your lunch.

1247
01:35:02.398 --> 01:35:04.537
The women folk are
coming here for their bath.

1248
01:35:04.634 --> 01:35:07.513
Would appreciate if you
could all step outside.

1249
01:35:07.570 --> 01:35:08.913
You too, please step outside.

1250
01:35:30.526 --> 01:35:32.904
Try it, it's very sweet.

1251
01:35:36.866 --> 01:35:38.140
Don't pray so hard...

1252
01:35:38.201 --> 01:35:40.181
lest the almighty himself come down.

1253
01:35:41.905 --> 01:35:44.715
And asks you to
accompany him back to heaven.

1254
01:35:56.552 --> 01:35:58.657
We've been betrayed.

1255
01:35:59.455 --> 01:36:01.833
Everybody take your position!

1256
01:36:21.411 --> 01:36:22.651
Give me cover.

1257
01:36:42.165 --> 01:36:43.371
What's wrong?

1258
01:36:46.836 --> 01:36:49.373
Balram, let the cattle loose.

1259
01:36:49.439 --> 01:36:50.884
Are you hurt, brother?

1260
01:36:54.877 --> 01:36:58.017
- Where have you been shot?
- My time is up.

1261
01:36:58.581 --> 01:37:01.027
- You leave now.
- I won't let you die.

1262
01:37:01.117 --> 01:37:02.687
My story is up.

1263
01:37:02.785 --> 01:37:04.731
I'll get you out of here.

1264
01:37:05.321 --> 01:37:06.527
Hold my hand.

1265
01:37:57.040 --> 01:37:58.576
Pull it, quick!

1266
01:37:58.775 --> 01:38:00.755
Quick, the cops
won't swim across.

1267
01:38:03.112 --> 01:38:05.092
Mark my words!

1268
01:38:05.148 --> 01:38:07.958
Don't come any closer or
you will be killed!

1269
01:38:34.577 --> 01:38:39.322
Three of our men have died.

1270
01:38:39.682 --> 01:38:41.684
Their bodies are with the police.

1271
01:38:45.955 --> 01:38:48.401
Inform their families and
send them money.

1272
01:38:50.359 --> 01:38:53.602
Tell them, I'll come to meet them.

1273
01:38:55.264 --> 01:38:57.266
We have to do something now.

1274
01:38:58.501 --> 01:38:59.775
What I?

1275
01:39:00.069 --> 01:39:01.309
Uncle...

1276
01:39:01.637 --> 01:39:05.414
Till I don't burn down that village...

1277
01:39:05.975 --> 01:39:08.285
I will get no solace.

1278
01:39:08.377 --> 01:39:09.913
Come here, son...

1279
01:39:11.981 --> 01:39:14.325
He was a father figure to me too.

1280
01:39:15.918 --> 01:39:18.626
Save your anger for the last round.

1281
01:39:19.822 --> 01:39:24.237
We'll teach them such a lesson,
nobody in Chambal will dare betray us.

1282
01:39:36.205 --> 01:39:38.651
This is the gang of
Paan Singh Tomar from Bhidosa.

1283
01:39:38.741 --> 01:39:40.914
We do not harm children and women.

1284
01:39:40.943 --> 01:39:42.513
But rest assured,
the informer cannot escape.

1285
01:39:42.612 --> 01:39:44.250
You bloody bastard, come outside.

1286
01:39:45.481 --> 01:39:46.755
What are you doing?!

1287
01:39:46.816 --> 01:39:48.625
Don't stop me, Subedaar uncle.

1288
01:39:48.684 --> 01:39:51.028
I won't spare anybody in the village.

1289
01:39:51.120 --> 01:39:52.224
Stop talking nonsense!

1290
01:39:52.321 --> 01:39:53.356
Give me the gun.

1291
01:39:53.456 --> 01:39:54.730
Get back now.

1292
01:39:54.824 --> 01:39:57.964
Go and get the headman
and his relatives...

1293
01:39:59.262 --> 01:40:00.935
Where do you think you're going?

1294
01:40:01.030 --> 01:40:02.338
Listen carefully.

1295
01:40:03.099 --> 01:40:05.773
This is the rule of
Paan Singh's gang.

1296
01:40:07.470 --> 01:40:10.747
We don't spare the
police and their informers.

1297
01:40:11.607 --> 01:40:13.587
But the poor and the innocent have

1298
01:40:13.643 --> 01:40:15.122
our complete protection.

1299
01:40:16.512 --> 01:40:17.991
Remember...

1300
01:40:18.548 --> 01:40:22.121
betraying us is an
invitation to death.

1301
01:40:23.753 --> 01:40:25.494
Forgive me, sir.

1302
01:40:26.756 --> 01:40:28.667
What do you have to say now?

1303
01:40:28.724 --> 01:40:30.601
- Forgive us.
- Forgive?

1304
01:40:31.627 --> 01:40:34.005
Like a dog you betrayed us
to the cops.

1305
01:40:34.096 --> 01:40:34.870
Say 'yes'.

1306
01:40:35.998 --> 01:40:38.103
- Say 'yes'.
- Yes.

1307
01:40:38.201 --> 01:40:40.408
You squealed and my pious brother...

1308
01:40:40.469 --> 01:40:42.210
paid with his life.

1309
01:40:42.271 --> 01:40:44.273
My mistake, forgive me.

1310
01:40:44.340 --> 01:40:46.342
How can I forgive you?

1311
01:40:46.442 --> 01:40:48.080
It was a mistake.

1312
01:41:17.306 --> 01:41:18.614
Satpal...

1313
01:41:19.008 --> 01:41:20.146
Satpal!

1314
01:41:22.612 --> 01:41:23.886
Yes, Sir!

1315
01:41:24.180 --> 01:41:26.888
Is this going to play all night?
Stop this blaring music!

1316
01:41:27.850 --> 01:41:29.329
Stop the music!

1317
01:41:30.052 --> 01:41:31.156
Just a minute.

1318
01:41:37.026 --> 01:41:40.564
Is your interview over?

1319
01:41:40.630 --> 01:41:42.473
- Yes, I'm done.
- Then go.

1320
01:41:45.134 --> 01:41:46.579
And one more thing...

1321
01:41:50.673 --> 01:41:51.845
Listen...

1322
01:41:52.675 --> 01:41:54.086
understand this...

1323
01:41:55.511 --> 01:41:57.650
it was necessary to kill...

1324
01:41:59.348 --> 01:42:01.294
those nine villagers.

1325
01:42:01.851 --> 01:42:03.262
If I didn't kill them...

1326
01:42:05.755 --> 01:42:08.167
They were unarmed
but they were not innocent...

1327
01:42:08.724 --> 01:42:10.032
Yes.

1328
01:42:10.359 --> 01:42:13.568
Paan Singh is not a murderer.

1329
01:42:14.897 --> 01:42:16.103
I agree.

1330
01:42:20.636 --> 01:42:23.344
Will you be promoted
for writing this story?

1331
01:42:24.507 --> 01:42:25.918
Yes.

1332
01:42:31.314 --> 01:42:34.056
Buy some sweets for your sister.

1333
01:42:35.885 --> 01:42:36.886
Go now.

1334
01:42:43.359 --> 01:42:45.805
There are so many
journalists trying...

1335
01:42:45.895 --> 01:42:48.273
and you say you managed it

1336
01:42:48.364 --> 01:42:50.742
Did you really meet Paan Singh?

1337
01:42:50.800 --> 01:42:52.473
Or did you just cook this up?

1338
01:42:52.568 --> 01:42:54.809
Small town mentality!

1339
01:42:54.904 --> 01:42:56.645
We had dinner together.

1340
01:42:56.739 --> 01:42:58.616
See how this shakes the government.

1341
01:43:20.863 --> 01:43:23.309
What are you doing?
Move them aside.

1342
01:43:23.399 --> 01:43:25.436
You know these animals...
they'll move on their own.

1343
01:43:25.534 --> 01:43:27.605
- What's the hurry?
- Why are you peeping inside?

1344
01:43:27.670 --> 01:43:28.740
Move on... move on...

1345
01:43:28.804 --> 01:43:32.013
I'm checking if one
round will be enough.

1346
01:43:35.978 --> 01:43:38.356
The killer of nine
innocent villagers...

1347
01:43:38.447 --> 01:43:42.520
dacoit Paan Singh Tomar was sitting
in Gwalior, calmly giving interviews.

1348
01:43:42.685 --> 01:43:44.824
The opposition has
slammed the government.

1349
01:43:50.426 --> 01:43:53.373
You didn't give us a chance to fire.

1350
01:43:53.429 --> 01:43:57.309
In this part of the world...
you shoot when you're in the mood.

1351
01:43:57.400 --> 01:43:59.038
I was in the mood today.

1352
01:43:59.101 --> 01:44:00.603
Open up the boot.

1353
01:44:03.973 --> 01:44:06.112
Inform his family.

1354
01:44:06.175 --> 01:44:06.812
Okay.

1355
01:44:06.909 --> 01:44:08.354
You can come out now.

1356
01:44:09.011 --> 01:44:11.321
Don't be scared,
These are real cops in real uniforms

1357
01:44:11.380 --> 01:44:12.450
Step out!

1358
01:44:18.954 --> 01:44:21.696
Back here again?
Get your act together...

1359
01:44:21.757 --> 01:44:23.293
- Sir!
- Yes

1360
01:44:28.097 --> 01:44:31.010
Paan Singh rules the Bhind area..

1361
01:44:31.434 --> 01:44:34.813
But his family and gang members...

1362
01:44:34.870 --> 01:44:36.315
hail from Morena.

1363
01:44:36.839 --> 01:44:40.218
I want Paan Singh to surrender.

1364
01:44:40.843 --> 01:44:43.756
After all,
he's been a national champion.

1365
01:44:44.980 --> 01:44:47.893
He used to win awards
for the country...

1366
01:44:48.350 --> 01:44:50.091
now there's a reward on his head.

1367
01:44:50.686 --> 01:44:52.359
Some people are in the mood for

1368
01:44:52.421 --> 01:44:53.900
an encounter, not surrender.

1369
01:45:50.379 --> 01:45:52.256
How did this happen, sir?

1370
01:45:52.314 --> 01:45:53.520
What's there to say!?

1371
01:45:53.582 --> 01:45:56.893
We were on the lookout for
Paan Singh's gang...

1372
01:45:56.952 --> 01:45:58.295
but got hold of another gang

1373
01:45:58.387 --> 01:46:00.333
now there is one less gang in the area

1374
01:46:06.295 --> 01:46:07.603
Greetings, Subedaar.

1375
01:46:18.874 --> 01:46:21.286
Ghesu and Pehelwan,
come with me.

1376
01:46:26.582 --> 01:46:27.925
Paan Singh...

1377
01:46:28.851 --> 01:46:30.990
the cops are getting
too close for comfort.

1378
01:46:31.654 --> 01:46:34.498
They killed ten members of the
Setu Mallah gang.

1379
01:46:34.590 --> 01:46:39.835
The nine villagers you killed...
and that interview...

1380
01:46:39.929 --> 01:46:42.034
has aggravated the matter.

1381
01:46:42.131 --> 01:46:45.772
What is it that you want?

1382
01:46:46.201 --> 01:46:49.205
You are the cause of these problems.

1383
01:46:49.905 --> 01:46:51.680
If you surrender...

1384
01:46:52.675 --> 01:46:54.086
things will be fine.

1385
01:47:03.218 --> 01:47:04.595
I'm not afraid...

1386
01:47:06.288 --> 01:47:09.132
If you are,
go surrender yourselves.

1387
01:47:09.224 --> 01:47:11.261
Don't be naive.

1388
01:47:12.027 --> 01:47:15.201
Surrender yourself
and things will be fine.

1389
01:47:20.869 --> 01:47:22.041
Sir...

1390
01:47:22.871 --> 01:47:24.680
Have you ever run a race?

1391
01:47:27.042 --> 01:47:29.079
There is a rule in racing.

1392
01:47:30.279 --> 01:47:32.190
Once the race begins...

1393
01:47:33.282 --> 01:47:35.888
regardless of whether
you win or lose...

1394
01:47:36.185 --> 01:47:38.165
you have to complete the race.

1395
01:47:38.954 --> 01:47:40.956
Over there on the horizon...

1396
01:47:41.056 --> 01:47:42.899
is the finish line.

1397
01:47:45.394 --> 01:47:46.839
You have to finish it.

1398
01:47:50.599 --> 01:47:54.445
Whether I win or lose...
I have to finish my race.

1399
01:47:55.037 --> 01:47:56.983
You think of yours.

1400
01:48:06.915 --> 01:48:09.191
What's the urgency?

1401
01:48:09.752 --> 01:48:12.392
I just feel like meeting them.

1402
01:48:13.822 --> 01:48:16.803
I don't want you to
go alone.

1403
01:48:16.892 --> 01:48:18.428
The police is looking
for me in the ravines...

1404
01:48:18.460 --> 01:48:19.996
but I'm going to town.

1405
01:48:22.431 --> 01:48:24.206
The police is looking
for a whole gang...

1406
01:48:25.267 --> 01:48:27.747
so we cannot stick together.

1407
01:48:28.704 --> 01:48:32.083
We'll all disperse in groups
of three or four.

1408
01:48:32.541 --> 01:48:33.849
Go far away from here.

1409
01:48:34.677 --> 01:48:37.487
We will meet a month from now
at the Goraiyya river bank.

1410
01:48:37.579 --> 01:48:38.853
A month from now.

1411
01:48:39.615 --> 01:48:40.685
Beware...

1412
01:48:41.116 --> 01:48:45.223
don't trust anyone
but your gang members.

1413
01:49:00.569 --> 01:49:02.378
Isn't this too high?

1414
01:49:02.471 --> 01:49:06.044
Paan Singh used to practice
at this height.

1415
01:49:19.388 --> 01:49:20.958
Stay right there...

1416
01:49:21.490 --> 01:49:23.265
Your colleagues shouldn't
get suspicious.

1417
01:49:23.325 --> 01:49:24.531
But, father...

1418
01:49:24.760 --> 01:49:28.674
Because now,
I'm not just a father...

1419
01:49:32.468 --> 01:49:33.879
You look smart.

1420
01:49:36.171 --> 01:49:37.980
Like an army man.

1421
01:49:38.040 --> 01:49:39.417
You've become weak.

1422
01:49:40.709 --> 01:49:42.052
I've grown old.

1423
01:49:44.246 --> 01:49:46.089
I got word of your marriage.

1424
01:49:48.550 --> 01:49:52.555
The girl is from Jalaun.

1425
01:49:53.689 --> 01:49:55.430
Mother has approved of her.

1426
01:49:55.491 --> 01:49:56.799
She has four brothers.

1427
01:49:56.859 --> 01:49:58.861
I hope my reputation
is not causing trouble.

1428
01:49:58.961 --> 01:50:00.668
They have agreed
because of you.

1429
01:50:01.897 --> 01:50:05.071
No one in their family
has had their pictures in the papers.

1430
01:50:06.235 --> 01:50:08.408
My disrepute is
of some use then...

1431
01:50:09.872 --> 01:50:13.217
How is your mother?

1432
01:50:13.275 --> 01:50:14.720
She worries about you.

1433
01:50:15.911 --> 01:50:18.949
Tell her I'll be coming to meet her.

1434
01:50:20.249 --> 01:50:21.421
Okay.

1435
01:50:23.252 --> 01:50:24.492
Go now.

1436
01:50:25.420 --> 01:50:26.455
Go...

1437
01:50:50.078 --> 01:50:52.922
Will you get into trouble
if you meet me?

1438
01:50:52.981 --> 01:50:54.756
If you are scared, I'll leave.

1439
01:50:54.817 --> 01:50:56.956
Who the hell is scared, dammit?!

1440
01:50:57.920 --> 01:50:59.922
- Why don't you do one thing?
- Yes.

1441
01:51:00.289 --> 01:51:02.530
Surrender yourself.

1442
01:51:04.293 --> 01:51:07.365
There's no other way out for you.

1443
01:51:07.462 --> 01:51:08.873
So I should accept that...

1444
01:51:08.964 --> 01:51:12.639
I made a mistake and seek forgiveness?

1445
01:51:14.269 --> 01:51:18.217
And be known as a surrendered
rebel for the rest of my life.

1446
01:51:19.441 --> 01:51:23.116
Why don't you ask this of the people
who make us rebels?!

1447
01:51:23.979 --> 01:51:25.549
Ask them to surrender first.

1448
01:51:25.614 --> 01:51:26.820
Then I will.

1449
01:51:34.990 --> 01:51:36.128
I am leaving now.

1450
01:51:36.491 --> 01:51:38.334
Don't mind me taking these.

1451
01:51:39.862 --> 01:51:41.398
I'm also taking this photograph.

1452
01:52:04.286 --> 01:52:08.029
So, why did you come here?

1453
01:52:09.124 --> 01:52:11.536
I missed your abuses.

1454
01:52:12.527 --> 01:52:15.133
Not sure if I will get another chance.

1455
01:52:17.332 --> 01:52:19.243
I missed you a lot.

1456
01:52:28.477 --> 01:52:29.581
Here he is.

1457
01:52:33.882 --> 01:52:35.452
Go ahead, eat some.

1458
01:52:39.321 --> 01:52:40.425
Janki...

1459
01:52:41.857 --> 01:52:43.165
this is for you.

1460
01:52:44.826 --> 01:52:48.501
What else has your astrologer
predicted about my future?

1461
01:52:48.563 --> 01:52:50.372
He said you will surrender.

1462
01:52:51.500 --> 01:52:53.377
That's all he can say...

1463
01:52:53.735 --> 01:52:55.578
Surrender... surrender.

1464
01:52:55.671 --> 01:52:57.446
Do you know what
it means to surrender?

1465
01:52:57.739 --> 01:53:00.686
He is just trying to please you.

1466
01:53:03.211 --> 01:53:04.383
Don't you worry.

1467
01:53:04.446 --> 01:53:07.290
This will settle down pretty soon.

1468
01:53:09.284 --> 01:53:11.059
When will you come again, father?

1469
01:53:12.220 --> 01:53:14.131
Whenever I happen to pass by.

1470
01:53:14.690 --> 01:53:16.169
Will you surrender yourself?

1471
01:53:16.224 --> 01:53:18.761
Your astrologer's definition
of surrender is different.

1472
01:53:18.860 --> 01:53:21.340
We all have to surrender some day.

1473
01:53:39.281 --> 01:53:40.988
No, no... it's alright.

1474
01:53:42.184 --> 01:53:43.322
Get me some water.

1475
01:53:43.418 --> 01:53:46.194
We are a lowly caste, sir.

1476
01:53:46.288 --> 01:53:48.393
Caste and creed are not important.

1477
01:53:49.124 --> 01:53:51.229
We should help each other.

1478
01:53:52.361 --> 01:53:55.103
Customs which create such
discrimination...

1479
01:53:55.197 --> 01:53:57.541
should be done away with.

1480
01:53:57.599 --> 01:53:58.907
Don't you agree?

1481
01:53:59.201 --> 01:54:02.148
When have you been wrong?!

1482
01:54:06.074 --> 01:54:07.576
Tell me...

1483
01:54:08.477 --> 01:54:11.651
this boy Gopi from Paan Singh's gang,
is this his wife's village?

1484
01:54:11.747 --> 01:54:12.953
Yes.

1485
01:54:13.515 --> 01:54:14.960
He comes here often?

1486
01:54:15.350 --> 01:54:17.057
Yes, he does.

1487
01:54:17.152 --> 01:54:19.189
He comes for social functions.

1488
01:54:19.287 --> 01:54:21.198
His wife lives here.

1489
01:54:21.790 --> 01:54:23.463
Get us to meet next time.

1490
01:54:25.927 --> 01:54:27.929
Would benefit both of you.

1491
01:54:28.030 --> 01:54:30.374
Will you enlist my son in the police?

1492
01:54:30.432 --> 01:54:32.275
Then it will benefit me.

1493
01:54:34.069 --> 01:54:35.776
Your wish is my command.

1494
01:54:36.738 --> 01:54:38.115
Won't need it now, son.

1495
01:54:38.440 --> 01:54:40.943
We'll celebrate your induction now.

1496
01:54:42.778 --> 01:54:45.122
It's important.
Should get sorted soon.

1497
01:54:45.781 --> 01:54:47.317
Sure. Will be done.

1498
01:54:49.651 --> 01:54:50.857
Goodbye, sir.

1499
01:54:57.726 --> 01:55:00.263
You are suddenly concerned about me.

1500
01:55:01.163 --> 01:55:02.107
Why?

1501
01:55:12.274 --> 01:55:14.618
And how would you do that?

1502
01:55:31.560 --> 01:55:33.369
I suggest we go to Rajasthan.

1503
01:55:33.428 --> 01:55:37.103
What's with Rajasthan?
Got a mistress out there?

1504
01:55:37.199 --> 01:55:38.041
We are not staying here.

1505
01:55:38.100 --> 01:55:40.376
We cross the border
tonight and go to U.P.

1506
01:55:40.435 --> 01:55:42.244
What's the harm
in staying a little longer.

1507
01:55:42.304 --> 01:55:43.612
Are you tired?

1508
01:55:43.705 --> 01:55:45.275
I've got some sweets for you.

1509
01:55:45.373 --> 01:55:46.875
We'll leave after eating it.

1510
01:55:47.242 --> 01:55:48.277
Hold on!

1511
01:55:51.646 --> 01:55:53.125
You eat it first.

1512
01:55:53.682 --> 01:55:56.856
Not this one,
take this other one.

1513
01:56:02.023 --> 01:56:04.367
This can be easily eaten
while walking.

1514
01:56:05.894 --> 01:56:08.204
Your mother-in-law
made this for us?

1515
01:56:08.263 --> 01:56:10.869
No, there was a wedding in
the village. I got it from there.

1516
01:56:12.601 --> 01:56:13.807
Subedaar...

1517
01:56:14.202 --> 01:56:16.808
there is a rich party
staying in the village.

1518
01:56:16.905 --> 01:56:17.940
It's a good opportunity.

1519
01:56:18.039 --> 01:56:20.212
We need to lie low for a few days.

1520
01:56:31.953 --> 01:56:33.364
What happened, sir?

1521
01:56:34.289 --> 01:56:38.533
People shouldn't think Paan
Singh's gang is afraid of the police.

1522
01:56:38.593 --> 01:56:40.573
This news has reached the papers.

1523
01:56:41.563 --> 01:56:43.907
Gopi, is the party really loaded?

1524
01:56:43.965 --> 01:56:46.571
The wedding is next Saturday.

1525
01:56:46.902 --> 01:56:50.509
We can kidnap at least
four or five people.

1526
01:56:51.139 --> 01:56:54.848
Sir, trust me,
we should go to Rajasthan.

1527
01:56:54.943 --> 01:56:57.355
We'll take our catch
and go to Rajasthan.

1528
01:56:57.445 --> 01:56:59.686
I refuse to be subdued
by the police.

1529
01:57:07.656 --> 01:57:10.899
Gopi, can we trust your wife's family?

1530
01:57:14.896 --> 01:57:16.637
They gave me their daughter.

1531
01:57:36.318 --> 01:57:40.095
- Subedaar, lets stop right here.
- But why?

1532
01:57:40.822 --> 01:57:42.859
Looks like the Grim Reaper.

1533
01:58:12.687 --> 01:58:14.360
- Gopi...
- Yes

1534
01:58:17.559 --> 01:58:19.732
Check if the coast is clear...

1535
01:58:20.228 --> 01:58:21.707
and bring the host here.

1536
01:58:21.763 --> 01:58:22.764
Okay.

1537
01:58:26.034 --> 01:58:27.069
Uncle...

1538
01:58:27.402 --> 01:58:28.847
I'm coming.

1539
01:58:29.571 --> 01:58:32.780
The gang's outside the village.
Subedaar's called for you.

1540
01:58:32.841 --> 01:58:35.822
- Son, go inform the inspector.
- I'll go get him.

1541
01:58:41.549 --> 01:58:42.960
This way.

1542
01:58:43.318 --> 01:58:45.821
You guys go ahead.

1543
01:58:45.887 --> 01:58:47.059
Govindram...

1544
01:58:49.257 --> 01:58:50.702
Are all the arrangements done?

1545
01:58:50.759 --> 01:58:53.968
I did my best
to organize what I could.

1546
01:58:54.062 --> 01:58:55.439
The fellows are tired.

1547
01:58:55.530 --> 01:58:58.704
We'll stay here for the night and
leave early morning with our catch.

1548
01:58:58.767 --> 01:59:00.007
Okay.

1549
01:59:00.101 --> 01:59:01.171
Where is Gopi?

1550
01:59:01.269 --> 01:59:02.976
I'm right here.

1551
01:59:06.775 --> 01:59:08.812
Leave early for the catch.

1552
01:59:11.279 --> 01:59:13.384
Get them out on some pretext

1553
01:59:13.481 --> 01:59:14.721
Okay.

1554
01:59:30.799 --> 01:59:33.109
- You got the booze?
- Yes.

1555
01:59:33.201 --> 01:59:34.441
The food is ready.

1556
01:59:34.502 --> 01:59:36.140
You will have to eat it first.

1557
01:59:36.971 --> 01:59:38.450
What do we do about this?

1558
01:59:39.074 --> 01:59:40.678
I'll say that I've quit.

1559
01:59:40.775 --> 01:59:42.516
Or I'll find some excuse.

1560
01:59:42.610 --> 01:59:44.214
Have you checked the sedatives?

1561
01:59:44.312 --> 01:59:45.814
Yes I have.

1562
01:59:45.947 --> 01:59:48.325
Subedaar shouldn't get suspicious.
Or we're dead

1563
01:59:48.383 --> 01:59:49.862
You quit!

1564
01:59:49.951 --> 01:59:51.760
- Sir. I quit.
- Why?

1565
01:59:51.853 --> 01:59:54.561
I had TB last year.

1566
01:59:55.690 --> 01:59:57.567
- That's enough for me.
- That's it?

1567
01:59:57.659 --> 01:59:58.797
That's my rule.

1568
01:59:58.893 --> 02:00:02.033
Alcohol is good in small amounts.
After that it is poison.

1569
02:00:02.430 --> 02:00:03.408
Give some to everyone.

1570
02:00:03.465 --> 02:00:04.409
Pass around the alcohol.

1571
02:00:04.466 --> 02:00:06.446
Tell them to have some.
They'll sleep well.

1572
02:00:06.501 --> 02:00:07.445
Will you have some?

1573
02:00:07.502 --> 02:00:08.503
No, no.

1574
02:00:27.655 --> 02:00:30.397
Life was a barren land.

1575
02:00:30.458 --> 02:00:33.098
Filled with loneliness and sorrow...

1576
02:00:34.462 --> 02:00:36.203
Till I met you

1577
02:00:36.297 --> 02:00:40.109
- Then?
-the rest of my life got screwed

1578
02:00:41.035 --> 02:00:42.571
Uncle...

1579
02:00:46.040 --> 02:00:47.883
- What happened?!
- I told you!

1580
02:00:47.942 --> 02:00:49.046
That death is in the air.

1581
02:00:49.110 --> 02:00:50.748
The bloody cops have surrounded
the entire village.

1582
02:00:50.812 --> 02:00:52.587
- The cops are here?
- Yes.

1583
02:00:53.214 --> 02:00:54.784
Give me my gun.

1584
02:00:54.883 --> 02:00:58.160
- Govindram!
- Yes, sir.

1585
02:00:58.620 --> 02:00:59.792
Who informed the cops?
Tell me who.

1586
02:00:59.854 --> 02:01:02.357
I don't know sir. Not me sir.

1587
02:01:02.457 --> 02:01:03.765
Tell me who.

1588
02:01:03.825 --> 02:01:05.463
I didn't do it.

1589
02:01:05.527 --> 02:01:07.302
Trust me, I didn't inform on you.

1590
02:01:08.229 --> 02:01:10.470
I don't want to go to hell.

1591
02:01:10.532 --> 02:01:12.307
I was...

1592
02:01:12.367 --> 02:01:13.778
I am obliged to you.

1593
02:01:13.868 --> 02:01:15.438
Where is the police?

1594
02:01:15.537 --> 02:01:16.743
At the canal.

1595
02:01:16.838 --> 02:01:18.181
Let the cattle loose!

1596
02:01:18.239 --> 02:01:21.049
The cop manning the LMG
won't hesitate to shoot them.

1597
02:01:21.543 --> 02:01:22.248
Call Gopi.

1598
02:01:22.310 --> 02:01:24.847
The bag of bullets is with him.

1599
02:01:24.913 --> 02:01:25.983
He has the bullets?

1600
02:01:26.047 --> 02:01:28.584
He ran away in the nick of time.

1601
02:01:29.384 --> 02:01:30.692
How many cops are there?

1602
02:01:30.752 --> 02:01:31.753
About 500.

1603
02:01:31.853 --> 02:01:34.265
There's only one way out of the
village and that's where the cops are.

1604
02:01:34.355 --> 02:01:35.925
We have to escape from there.

1605
02:01:36.391 --> 02:01:37.267
Get the megaphone.

1606
02:01:37.392 --> 02:01:38.803
It's ready!

1607
02:01:39.594 --> 02:01:41.005
We leave this way.

1608
02:01:42.163 --> 02:01:43.141
Where's my gun?!

1609
02:01:43.231 --> 02:01:45.233
Everyone go towards the canal.

1610
02:01:45.266 --> 02:01:47.075
Stay together.

1611
02:01:47.135 --> 02:01:48.842
We move ahead in a scout formation.

1612
02:01:48.937 --> 02:01:50.814
Keep moving in this formation.

1613
02:02:32.580 --> 02:02:34.059
He's been shot.

1614
02:02:35.683 --> 02:02:36.855
Get down!

1615
02:02:55.970 --> 02:02:57.711
Don't shoot me.

1616
02:02:57.805 --> 02:03:00.342
I'm the informer Gopi!

1617
02:03:00.441 --> 02:03:01.351
Bloody traitor

1618
02:03:01.442 --> 02:03:02.978
Don't shoot.

1619
02:03:03.044 --> 02:03:04.853
Hold your fire!

1620
02:03:23.998 --> 02:03:25.477
Somebody man the LMG.

1621
02:03:28.503 --> 02:03:30.847
- Who got shot?
- Govind.

1622
02:03:31.005 --> 02:03:32.882
- Where?
- He's dead.

1623
02:03:40.248 --> 02:03:44.253
There's only one way out.

1624
02:03:49.958 --> 02:03:51.801
We have to cross the canal.

1625
02:03:52.493 --> 02:03:54.200
That's my route.

1626
02:03:54.762 --> 02:03:55.832
They will attack me...

1627
02:03:55.930 --> 02:03:58.035
Try running away through the fields!

1628
02:03:59.100 --> 02:04:00.841
Subedaar...
What's the matter, Subedaar?

1629
02:04:00.902 --> 02:04:04.509
I think the bastard
poisoned the drinks.

1630
02:04:06.708 --> 02:04:08.415
Subedaar...

1631
02:04:08.943 --> 02:04:10.081
Subedaar...

1632
02:04:10.178 --> 02:04:12.055
Are you feeling drugged, Jigesh?

1633
02:04:13.781 --> 02:04:15.419
Where are you going?

1634
02:04:16.084 --> 02:04:17.495
Where are you going?

1635
02:04:29.864 --> 02:04:31.104
Subedaar...

1636
02:04:33.368 --> 02:04:34.574
Subedaar...

1637
02:05:23.384 --> 02:05:25.955
Inform the CM that
the operation is a success.

1638
02:05:26.621 --> 02:05:28.430
Go and count the bodies.

1639
02:05:29.057 --> 02:05:31.264
We are yet to find Paan Singh's body.

1640
02:05:32.927 --> 02:05:35.271
Go and find him...

1641
02:05:35.863 --> 02:05:40.903
Subedaar, it's all over.
Everyone's dead.

1642
02:05:44.338 --> 02:05:46.875
- You are still alive Ramcharan.
- Yes.

1643
02:05:50.445 --> 02:05:52.356
There lies the finish line.

1644
02:05:55.183 --> 02:05:57.891
The canal is the final hurdle.

1645
02:06:03.491 --> 02:06:05.402
Tell people my story.

1646
02:06:06.994 --> 02:06:11.101
That Paan Singh finished his race.

1647
02:06:12.100 --> 02:06:14.011
He did not surrender.

1648
02:06:14.869 --> 02:06:16.906
We shall meet again.

1649
02:06:25.947 --> 02:06:27.290
Ramcharan!

1650
02:06:48.302 --> 02:06:51.340
Listen here, corrupt inspector...

1651
02:06:52.840 --> 02:06:55.081
This gang isn't finished yet.

1652
02:06:55.877 --> 02:06:57.982
Paan Singh is alive.

1653
02:06:58.679 --> 02:07:00.716
And he will never surrender!

1654
02:07:01.949 --> 02:07:06.762
Many before you tried to catch me
but failed miserably.

1655
02:07:07.088 --> 02:07:08.863
And you think you will?!

1656
02:07:09.524 --> 02:07:12.232
Bring in some more
battalions to help you...

1657
02:07:13.895 --> 02:07:16.273
try and capture Paan Singh!
